    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6042913378480130
    m_Localized: 'Story: coming soon'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6042913378480131
    m_Localized: Story mode
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6042913378480132
    m_Localized: Endless mode
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6042913378480133
    m_Localized: All aboard!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604498214912
    m_Localized: A BLANK LEGACY
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963648
    m_Localized: "My name is Faceless. Here they usually add \u201Cthe champion\u201D
      and expect a greeting. I oblige, of course. I worry someone might think I am
      ignoring them; my face does little to clarify things."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963649
    m_Localized: My work is to compete and destroy whoever I am directed toward.
      Before leaving I ask if it is necessary. The answer usually includes coordinates,
      so I put my sketchbook away and go. I dislike admitting how well I learned
      the job.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963650
    m_Localized: My father was champion before me, and my grandfather before him.
      At home they discussed victories like travel memories. I would ask what the
      places looked like, and they would explain how they had won there.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963651
    m_Localized: I love them and did not want to disappoint them. I accepted the
      locomotive, the training and the title. I kept postponing the conversation
      about wanting another life until a quieter moment. There always seemed to be
      a ceremony first.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963652
    m_Localized: What I enjoy is drawing. I can spend an afternoon studying how a
      leaf folds. Then someone asks if I am planning a strategy. I show them the
      sketch. I have not yet convinced everyone it was only a leaf.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963653
    m_Localized: I would like to learn without watching the clock between assignments.
      To draw people sitting still because they are comfortable, not because I have
      just defeated them. For now I practice with what I find beside the tracks.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963654
    m_Localized: My best friend is T.exe, my locomotive. She is alive and has quite
      a personality. When I show her a sketch, she leans closer. I devoted an entire
      sketchbook to her; she maintains I made her chimney too short.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963655
    m_Localized: We enjoy traveling together. What exhausts me is every journey having
      to end in a fight. I told her one night in the cab, my sketchbook on my knees.
      T.exe waited until I finished and brought the light a little closer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963656
    m_Localized: After that I began keeping even the drawings that went wrong. I
      used to discard them out of embarrassment. Now I like revisiting what I was
      trying to do. T.exe keeps some in the cab. I asked her not to display them
      during inspections.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963657
    m_Localized: When war was announced, more assignments arrived and our routes
      changed. I heard my boss promise the champion would handle the invaders. I
      would have liked to be present when I volunteered.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963658
    m_Localized: I did not want to keep hurting people, but I did not know how to
      say I was leaving. I rehearsed a resignation with T.exe. It sounded so solemn
      I ended up apologizing to the door. She waited. I tried again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963659
    m_Localized: Then I thought about the title. If they needed a champion who always
      won, perhaps a defeat would let me leave. I explained it to T.exe. She did
      not seem impressed, but had already brought my sketchbook closer to plan the
      performance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963660
    m_Localized: Hey, tall fellow! Will you let me through, or do you want the rock
      too? Because I am getting tired of explaining it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963661
    m_Localized: Good afternoon. I am Faceless. I was assigned to stop you, and I
      would prefer neither of us be hurt. Could we begin by leaving some room between
      the engines?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963662
    m_Localized: Excuse me a moment. T.exe, we have won again. I think we rehearsed
      the wrong part.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6071604535963663
    m_Localized: BBA left without asking for another fight. I kept performing my
      defeat until T.exe let me know she was no longer watching. She helped me back
      up. I had prepared everything except a dignified recovery.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477405220864
    m_Localized: Thank you. And, if you would not mind, please avoid the cab. Some
      drawings are drying there. Yes, I understand that is not the most urgent matter;
      I wanted to ask anyway.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477451358208
    m_Localized: Oh, noooooooo! You defeated me! I can no longer follow you! Please
      go ahead. I will handle the report.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477451358209
    m_Localized: Oh! Yes, yes, I beat you completely. Thanks for... that. See you,
      Mister Artist!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552512
    m_Localized: "It was not convincing acting. During \u201COh, noooooooo!\u201D
      I waved so hard I nearly dropped the sketchbook. But she agreed to leave, and
      nobody had to remain hurt on the tracks. For my debut, I was content with that."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552513
    m_Localized: "I drafted a resignation explaining that a driver from Earth had
      surpassed the champion. I crossed out \u201Csurpassed\u201D and wrote \u201Cdefeated\u201D;
      my boss rarely appreciates nuance. Then I asked T.exe to take me there to deliver
      it."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552514
    m_Localized: A RESIGNATION REJECTED
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552515
    m_Localized: We returned to the station with the resignation neatly folded. T.exe
      stopped closer to the window so I would not have to raise my voice. I thanked
      her. Asking for something for myself was proving difficult.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552516
    m_Localized: Before seeing me they needed to check I was not an infiltrating
      human. I greeted the officer and put away my sketchbook to listen. T.exe waited
      outside. I signaled that it would take a moment; I did not want her thinking
      I had changed my mind.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552517
    m_Localized: When I reached my boss, I handed over the resignation and described
      my defeat. Then I added that I wanted to draw. He glanced at the paper and
      set it down unread. I stood with my hands together, waiting for a question.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552518
    m_Localized: "\u201CYou will not resign in the middle of a war.\u201D That was
      all. Another invader was near the fortress and I was to stop him. I took my
      resignation back before leaving; there was a drawing on the reverse, and I
      did not want it discarded."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552519
    m_Localized: T.exe took me to the fortress. On the way I told her what happened
      and asked her to be careful. She could compete for hours; I only wanted us
      to find a way out without destroying anyone this time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552520
    m_Localized: Faceless. Easy. I need to cross, not take your head as a souvenir.
      Tell me your orders and we will find a way out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552521
    m_Localized: Good afternoon, Cerebron. So would I. My boss still wants me to
      stop you, though I would prefer neither of us needing a workshop afterward.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552522
    m_Localized: Incidentally, a profile portrait would suit you very well. Forgive
      me, that was poorly timed. I am listening.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552523
    m_Localized: Thank you for the game. If I say over the radio that reinforcements
      were coming, would you mind not correcting me yet? I need to get away from
      here.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552524
    m_Localized: I heard nothing. Get going. I will watch the entrance, and you owe
      me no more explanations.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552525
    m_Localized: Cerebron stopped arguing and I put away the board. I would have
      liked to stay and draw, but I still owed my boss a report. T.exe moved toward
      the exit while I searched for a way to explain I would not return to my post.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552526
    m_Localized: In the end I announced reinforcements Cerebron had never mentioned.
      I said we would intercept them. Using his name felt wrong, though he did not
      contradict me. I kept the radio on until permission came and thanked him quietly.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552527
    m_Localized: Before departure I asked T.exe whether she wanted to come. I did
      not want my escape to become another order for her. She positioned herself
      under the launcher and opened the cab. I climbed in with my sketchbook; we
      discussed destinations only once far away.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552528
    m_Localized: OUTSIDE THE FRAME
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552529
    m_Localized: We made it away from the planet. I was sketching the curve of the
      tracks from the cab when the radio sounded again. They wanted a more precise
      position. I lowered my pencil and looked at T.exe before replying.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552530
    m_Localized: I finally said I would not return. I was respectful; I even thanked
      them again for my training. The reply was an order to stop. This time I let
      the silence stand without promising to obey.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552531
    m_Localized: Soon afterward the creature covered in eyes appeared. Together they
      seemed to follow T.exe's every movement. I put the unfinished sketch away.
      Being watched while working makes me uncomfortable, especially by someone there
      to stop me leaving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552532
    m_Localized: The champion must return. Stop that locomotive.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552533
    m_Localized: I am sorry for the trouble, but I will not return. Please let my
      friend through. She chose to come too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552534
    m_Localized: We can move away now, T.exe. Let me check your cab. The sketchbook
      can wait; you should not have to take another hit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552535
    m_Localized: I suggested Earth. From the radio I knew they were occupied with
      war too, but I knew nowhere else we could land without returning to my boss.
      I asked T.exe to find a quiet track. I would help find somewhere to stay.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552536
    m_Localized: "As we approached, I saw debris crossing the descent route. I secured
      the drawers and held my sketchbook under one arm. \u201CSlowly, if you can,\u201D
      I asked. Then I saw what followed us and added that she need not take it literally."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552537
    m_Localized: AN ALIEN WITHOUT AN APPOINTMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552538
    m_Localized: We reached Earth and I waited beside T.exe. I assumed someone would
      ask who we were. I had prepared a short explanation. Short, at least, until
      the part about the drawings.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552539
    m_Localized: Nobody came. There were birds over the tracks and light between
      the trees I immediately wanted to sketch. First I asked whether T.exe needed
      rest. We had traveled a long way to stand still looking at leaves.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552540
    m_Localized: We continued looking for somewhere to stop without being in the
      way. I was considering how to ask permission to use a cabin when another locomotive
      appeared. Its driver did have questions, although he spoke too quickly to let
      me introduce myself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552541
    m_Localized: I was sent to stop you! When I defeat the alien invader, everyone
      will see I am a hero!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552542
    m_Localized: I understand this matters to you. I was a champion and became very
      tired. Would you let me explain why we are here before we begin?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552543
    m_Localized: I am sorry you were hurt. I did not come to conquer anything. My
      friend and I want somewhere safe to live; if you need help clearing your engine
      from the track, I can stay a moment.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552544
    m_Localized: Live here? That is all? You could have started with that. Now I
      must explain why there is no invasion.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552545
    m_Localized: I left him beside his locomotive after checking he could continue.
      He did not seem to want more conversation. I understood and said goodbye. T.exe
      was waiting; she too needed some time without someone trying to defeat her.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552546
    m_Localized: In the towns everyone wore clothes. I thought I should acquire a
      suit once we found a home. I did not want to stand out. T.exe pointed out my
      height, so I postponed that particular ambition.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552547
    m_Localized: There was still the tie. Blue might be more discreet, although I
      liked red. I drew two sketches to compare. Then a third in different light.
      T.exe had to remind me we still needed somewhere to sleep.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552548
    m_Localized: A CORNER OF MY OWN
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552549
    m_Localized: I found a forest cabin where I could leave my sketchbook open and
      return the next day. I hung drawings among the trees to see them in natural
      light. T.exe said the wind tilted them. I rather liked the result.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552550
    m_Localized: One night I saw flashlights among the trees and children taking
      the pages down. I was pleased they had stopped to look until they began carrying
      them away. I went out to ask for them back; they ran before I finished greeting
      them.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552551
    m_Localized: Emerging from the shadows waving my arms probably did not help.
      They are frightened, and I need the pages back without making it worse. I will
      approach carefully. The flower drawing has a stain on the back; I would hate
      them to think I gave it away like that.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552552
    m_Localized: Excuse me. Those pages are mine. I will not hurt you; I would just
      like them back, please.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552553
    m_Localized: Thank you for returning them. If you would like a drawing, you may
      ask. I would like to prepare one for you, without stains.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552554
    m_Localized: I hung the pages back up and left a note offering drawings to anyone
      who wanted to ask. I checked the lettering several times; I wanted it to look
      like an invitation. Then I went inside to clean the stain on the flower drawing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552555
    m_Localized: I am still drawing here. I do not really know why the war began
      or how it will end, and an unfamiliar locomotive still unsettles me. I put
      my sketchbook down and wait. Usually it passes by, and I can return to my work.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552556
    m_Localized: I would prefer my former boss not find this place. Learning to draw
      it and deciding where to hang my suit keeps me busy enough. I chose the red
      tie, incidentally. There was nothing wrong with blue; that made the decision
      terribly difficult.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552557
    m_Localized: T.exe changed shape and found work. She now looks like an Earth
      locomotive; she let me draw her before her first shift. Again she corrected
      my chimney. I thanked her and started another page.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552558
    m_Localized: I have seen children greet her before boarding. She waits until
      everyone is seated, then leaves making a very satisfied noise. Whenever I ask
      about work, she has something to tell me. I enjoy listening.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552559
    m_Localized: We meet after her shift. Sometimes we talk about our journeys; sometimes
      she stays nearby while I draw. I usually bring the page closer for her opinion.
      Today she looked at it for quite a while. I think I got the chimney right this
      time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552560
    m_Localized: Earth is below us, T.exe. I will secure the drawers. Find us a safe
      route; the cloud sketch can wait.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552561
    m_Localized: We are down. Thank you, T.exe. Let us find a track where you can
      rest before continuing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552562
    m_Localized: 'Descent: {0}%'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552563
    m_Localized: THOSE ARE MY DRAWINGS!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552564
    m_Localized: 'Tonight, the monster in the forest is you. Take back your 8 drawings
      before dawn: 5 are carried by children with torches and 3 are pinned to trees.
      Come up from behind or out of the dark; if a torch lights you up the panic
      grows, and when it is full they run off with your pages. Careful: now and then
      they stop (?) and look back, and they hear you running close by. Every drawing
      you take back makes them warier.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552565
    m_Localized: "WASD / Stick: move   \xB7   Mouse / right stick / Q E: turn   \xB7  
      Shift / R2: run   \xB7   Space / X: take back"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552566
    m_Localized: 'X / Space: ''That drawing is mine, please'''
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552567
    m_Localized: 'Drawings recovered: {0} / {1}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552568
    m_Localized: "Dawn in {0}s   \xB7   Energy {1}%"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552569
    m_Localized: MY DRAWINGS ARE SAFE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552570
    m_Localized: They are all here. I will leave them to dry and prepare a drawing
      for anyone who asks. This time I will put up a sign before coming out to greet
      anyone.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552571
    m_Localized: THEY GOT AWAY WITH MY PAGES
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6170477455552572
    m_Localized: Dawn has come and some pages are missing. I hope I did not frighten
      them too much. I will look again when I can approach more carefully.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6172046045556736
    m_Localized: Recover my drawings
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6172046074916864
    m_Localized: Begin descent
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6175109212876800
    m_Localized: DESCENT FAILED
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6175109246431232
    m_Localized: I am sorry, T.exe. We took too many hits. I will check what happened
      before trying again; I do not want you descending like this.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065147006976
    m_Localized: Holo-Duel
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755712
    m_Localized: '{0} challenges you to a Holo-Duel'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755713
    m_Localized: Your turn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755714
    m_Localized: '{0}''s turn'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755715
    m_Localized: Beast
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755716
    m_Localized: Warrior
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755717
    m_Localized: Mage
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755718
    m_Localized: '{0}: +2 against {1}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755719
    m_Localized: '{0} beats {1}!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755720
    m_Localized: How to play
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755721
    m_Localized: 'Move one piece one cell a turn. Move into a rival piece to attack:
      both roll a die and the kind with the edge adds +2. The higher number takes
      a life off the other (each piece has 2); a tie, nobody loses one. Take all
      3 rival pieces. If the {0} moves run out, whoever has more lives wins; a tie
      counts as a loss.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755722
    m_Localized: '[W][A][S][D] / [LS] cell    [Space] / [xA] pick and move    [Esc]
      / [xB] let go'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755723
    m_Localized: You beat {0} at the Holo-Duel!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6284065184755724
    m_Localized: '{0} won the Holo-Duel'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6285937660473344
    m_Localized: Then leave the weapons idle and bring out the Holo-Duel. You get
      a battle to report; I keep my parts. Let us see how you move those pieces.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6285937689833472
    m_Localized: If we do not want one of us to die, a battle of wits is best. A
      Holo-Duel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6289036265467904
    m_Localized: pick one of your pieces
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6289036290633728
    m_Localized: "pick where it goes \xB7 green: good odds, red: bad odds"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6289036290633729
    m_Localized: "Your {0} \xB7 +2 against {1} \xB7 lives: {2}"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6289036290633730
    m_Localized: "{2}'s {0} \xB7 +2 against {1} \xB7 lives: {3}"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6289036290633731
    m_Localized: '{0} moves left'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6290823248687104
    m_Localized: "Win {0}% \xB7 tie {1}% \xB7 lose {2}%"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6290823273852928
    m_Localized: Your {0}
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6290823273852929
    m_Localized: '{1}''s {0}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6290823273852930
    m_Localized: '{0} wins the roll: {1} loses a life'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6290823273852931
    m_Localized: '{0} wins: {1} leaves the board'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6290823273852932
    m_Localized: A tie! Nobody loses a life
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6291412355461120
    m_Localized: Rolling the dice!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6465130474057728
    m_Localized: 'A tie: play it again!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6469827293425664
    m_Localized: 'Space / X: take the drawing off the tree'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6469827318591488
    m_Localized: Panic
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6469827318591489
    m_Localized: I frightened them and they took the drawings. Running after them
      did not help. I will have to give them room and try more calmly.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909045256192
    m_Localized: DIVINE CARD DECLINED
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199232
    m_Localized: Xiuhtecuhtli! That is me. Demigod, R-20 driver and, until recently,
      someone with access to things I did not have to pay for. My father cut off
      my premium card. Without warning. Well, there were warnings, but I was organizing
      a party.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199233
    m_Localized: He told me not to return until I became a hero. A hero! I already
      knew how to enter a room and make everyone look. What else did he need? I blame
      that Hercules film he watched. Before that he never made me solve mortals'
      problems.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199234
    m_Localized: So I ended up in the jungle explaining my situation to everyone
      passing by. Nobody knew how many heroic deeds I needed. One asked me to lower
      my voice. I told him I was trying to save my future; he could bear a little
      enthusiasm.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199235
    m_Localized: "Then government men arrived. They offered me the chance to save
      the planet by delivering a green rock to an alien base. I asked them to put
      \u201Csave the planet\u201D in writing. Father would want proof, surely. I
      already wanted to announce it."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199236
    m_Localized: "I will not pretend I heard the whole explanation. Once they said
      \u201Chero,\u201D I was imagining my welcome. My entrance, Father rising, everyone
      applauding... I even practiced my greeting while they spoke. Then I had to
      ask what color the rock was."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199237
    m_Localized: First I had to leave the jungle. I boarded R-20 and asked them to
      clear the way. Someone commented on its size. It is a perfectly adequate locomotive!
      I got down to explain, because I would not begin my heroic life tolerating
      such things.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199238
    m_Localized: Excuse me, is the city this way? I am looking for somewhere serving
      food, and nobody agrees on the directions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199239
    m_Localized: That is exactly where I am going, future legend of this planet!
      But I will not let you overtake me while I explain the way. All I will say
      is... Sayonara!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199240
    m_Localized: Ah. You wanted a fight. You could have started there and skipped
      the introduction.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199241
    m_Localized: Good! As the winner and a very busy person, I inform you that the
      city is that way. Yes, that way. There is no need to follow me to check.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199242
    m_Localized: Thanks. Although you are going the other... Well, I will try that
      way.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199243
    m_Localized: I gave her the wrong direction on purpose. There, I said it. I wanted
      to arrive first, and she could follow the real route. As I left I tried deciding
      whether that counted as strategy. Having to think about it so much annoyed
      me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199244
    m_Localized: Then I announced over the radio that I was heading to the city.
      Nobody had asked, but people must know where a hero is. They told me to clear
      the channel. I was providing useful information! I cleared it, after finishing
      my name.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199245
    m_Localized: FIRST, BUT NOT CHOSEN
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199246
    m_Localized: At the entrance I had to wait for a human questionnaire. I explained
      I was a demigod. There was no box for that. I offered to write it in the margin;
      they refused. I agreed to answer so they could sooner apologize for wasting
      my time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199247
    m_Localized: The launcher was in the city. I only had to arrive first, so I rehearsed
      my space-launch speech. I had shortened it. It would fit between two radio
      notices, provided everyone else did not insist on speaking too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199248
    m_Localized: Power remains for one launch. First to arrive gets the last trip
      to space. Keep access clear.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199249
    m_Localized: Exactly, clear it! I am coming! And remember who arrived first;
      people forget the important things afterward.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199250
    m_Localized: First! I said it and did it! Now activate it. I am in position.
      Activate it, I said!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199251
    m_Localized: I arrived first and waited. I even greeted the operators to help
      the ceremony along. Nothing. I shouted that the winner was inside. One measured
      my locomotive again. Measure it for what? I had already crossed the finish!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199252
    m_Localized: They said it was too small. That got me out. I explained the size
      of my victory, the effort involved and my opinion of their instruments. Quickly
      and loudly, because they were already preparing another engine and nobody gave
      me a decent answer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199253
    m_Localized: They chose BBA. The witch! They moved me aside with the rock still
      aboard, and I saw her climb toward the launcher. I kept saying I had won. By
      the time I got back to my engine, I had neither audience nor journey. Still
      the rock; nobody wanted that back.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199254
    m_Localized: A HERO ADRIFT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199255
    m_Localized: I went toward the sea looking for another way out and someone who
      owed me an explanation. I had been arguing over the radio when they cut me
      off. I could complain in person too! I just needed to find where.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199256
    m_Localized: Then I saw a blue and yellow locomotive. BBA. Had they not just
      given her my launch? I did not even understand what she was doing there, but
      I was already approaching to ask. To ask, and make certain she heard me this
      time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199257
    m_Localized: Hey, feather duster! You are crowding my track. If you have something
      to say, say it from yours.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199258
    m_Localized: They gave you my launch! I won! And now here you are, perfectly
      relaxed. I want someone to explain what is happening without telling me to
      be quiet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199259
    m_Localized: And do not call me feather duster! My name is Xiuhtecuhtli. If you
      are going to talk about me, learn to say it before you lose.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199260
    m_Localized: Fine, you won. Can I breathe now? I was not operating that launcher.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199261
    m_Localized: 'I know that! ...No, wait. I did not know. I am still angry, but
      stay there a moment: I am trying to sort out my reasons.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199262
    m_Localized: I won and still could not reach space. That made me angrier. I had
      done everything asked! Well, listening to instructions was debatable, but I
      had arrived first perfectly. I began addressing Father although the radio was
      off.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199263
    m_Localized: "\u201CThen I will be the villain, Father! Let us see if they listen
      now!\u201D I decided to throw the rock into Tzmil's volcano and repeated it
      until it sounded reasonable. Then I switched the radio on to announce it. My
      great decision needed witnesses."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199264
    m_Localized: THE SISTER AND THE VOLCANO
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199265
    m_Localized: I reached the volcano with my speech prepared and the rock on display.
      Tzmil approached without shouting. That unsettled me. I was ready for an argument,
      not to be asked how I was.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199266
    m_Localized: I tried explaining everything at once. The longer I spoke, the louder
      I became. My sister let me finish and asked me to move the rock away. I held
      it tighter. Her kindness after what I had announced made me angry.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199267
    m_Localized: Tzmil, do not make me explain again! I am throwing the rock! If
      I cannot return a hero, at least they will remember me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199268
    m_Localized: Brother, look at me a moment. Those people haven't hurt you. We
      can talk about the launcher, but I need you to move the rock away from the
      crater.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199269
    m_Localized: They took my chance! And now you ask me to calm down as though I
      merely lost a game. It was my way home!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199270
    m_Localized: If you're not ready to talk yet, let's play. I can wait, but the
      rock stays well away from the volcano.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199271
    m_Localized: 'I can see you can beat me. Now please hear what I''m asking: don''t
      hurt those people. I don''t want to lose you over this.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199272
    m_Localized: All right. I will move it away. But I am still angry! ...Not with
      you. Give me a moment, and stop using that voice; I cannot keep arguing when
      you do.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199273
    m_Localized: I moved the rock away and sat beside my sister. I still had an answer
      for everything, but wanted less and less to say them. She stayed near. When
      I promised not to throw it, I repeated it more quietly so she would believe
      me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199274
    m_Localized: I decided to return the rock. I would tell the government what I
      thought of their competition, of course, but explode nothing. Tzmil asked me
      to wait. I was already boarding R-20; I wanted it settled before another idea
      occurred.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199275
    m_Localized: I radioed that I was bringing their rock back. They ordered me to
      stop. Now that I was trying to fix things! I suppose they remembered the volcano
      and missed my change of plans. I explained again, louder each time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199276
    m_Localized: THE SPARE HERO
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199277
    m_Localized: "\u201CMaximum security emergency! Stop him!\u201D That greeted
      me. I shouted I was making a return. They repeated the warning, so I repeated
      myself too; if they could use loudspeakers, I could use every breath I had."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199278
    m_Localized: 'I searched the hangars for someone who could deal with me. I found
      soldiers, machines and, finally, another me. I was silent a moment. Very briefly.
      As soon as he moved I demanded explanations: they had not even had the decency
      to tell me.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199279
    m_Localized: Leave the cargo and stop. I am your replacement. Your data is already
      part of the project.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199280
    m_Localized: My replacement? I have exclusive rights to my outrage! You copied
      all of me and still could not give me one miserable launch?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909087199281
    m_Localized: If they had let you leave, they could not have finished. They needed
      to keep you here. The other drivers too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393536
    m_Localized: They could have asked! I would have said no, obviously, but you
      ask. And move my locomotive. The other one! Yours! You have even made that
      complicated.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393537
    m_Localized: You can destroy this copy. It was not the only one planned.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393538
    m_Localized: Enough copies! I want names, files and whoever had this idea standing
      in front of me. I am not leaving with another half explanation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393539
    m_Localized: I found the files after defeating my copy. Driver records, body
      scans and orders to manufacture soldiers from them. I searched myself first.
      Yes, myself first; I wanted to know how many versions of that idiot they intended
      to build.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393540
    m_Localized: The competition appeared in those documents too. They gathered us
      to study and detain us while making copies. More than one BBA was recorded.
      I thought of the witch at sea. And I had wasted time arguing with her while
      they continued this!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393541
    m_Localized: 'I read on: the alien shipments were silicon trade. There were plans
      to conquer those traders with clones and orders for BBA and Cerebron to weaken
      their military base. Nothing resembled the mission I had been sold.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393542
    m_Localized: I began shouting without waiting for an answer. The rock was in
      my hands; I saw an open shaft and threw it. I checked nothing and never considered
      the damage. When soldiers ran, I tried following. The floor was already shaking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393543
    m_Localized: I heard the explosion. I do not remember how I arrived afterward,
      but I was with Father at a long long table. He made room. I still wanted to
      explain what happened; he asked me to sit. This time I sat without arguing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393544
    m_Localized: I did not see Tzmil. I asked about her before tasting the food.
      I did not know whether she had escaped the base; nobody explained where she
      was. I left a place beside mine. When she appeared I would listen; I owed her
      more than an explanation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393545
    m_Localized: Father served me and stayed beside me. I had prepared so many speeches
      I did not know which to begin. I asked if I could stay a while. While waiting
      for his reply I began telling him about the journey. From the beginning, even
      if he interrupted.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393546
    m_Localized: Xiuhtecuhtli Clone
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393547
    m_Localized: 'First! Launch denied: machine too small.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393548
    m_Localized: Government Base
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6486909091393549
    m_Localized: Security War Rig
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128633700352
    m_Localized: HELL'S REBEL
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032000
    m_Localized: "I was born in hell, and even there people insist on telling you
      how to live. Don't cross here, don't go out there\u2026 Show me a forbidden
      door and I'd spend the rest of the day wondering what was on the other side."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032001
    m_Localized: "I wanted enough power to leave whenever I liked, and for people
      outside to know my name. Mostly, though, I wanted to see what was out there:
      cities, fights, food I'd never tried\u2026 Whenever someone described a trip,
      I wanted in."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032002
    m_Localized: So I slipped out a couple of times. I'm not telling you where through,
      or they'll close it, but one trip took me to a wrestling arena. I'd gone to
      watch and ended up asking when I could get in the ring.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032003
    m_Localized: And I liked it. They let you fight, gave you a belt if you won,
      and people actually wanted you back. I was happy, except I still had to return
      to hell and find another way out before the next show.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032004
    m_Localized: Then some people from Earth's government contacted me. They said
      they could get me out if I took a green rock to an alien base. I asked how
      far away it was, and while they explained, I was already thinking about what
      I could see along the way.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032005
    m_Localized: I accepted before they could change their minds. I'd work out the
      delivery when I got there; for now I had a trip out of hell and an engine waiting.
      They only needed to open the exit. There'd be time for instructions later.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032006
    m_Localized: Look who's here. Sneaking out again, Onini? You're carrying a lot
      for someone coming back before dinner.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032007
    m_Localized: This one's a long trip, witch. They're even paying me to carry a
      rock. Come along if you like, but don't block the exit. I'm not staying to
      ask permission.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032008
    m_Localized: Then make yourself a gap! Let's see how relaxed you are with RicMar
      beside you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032009
    m_Localized: There's my exit. See? If you wanted to say goodbye that badly, you
      could've done it without shooting.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032010
    m_Localized: You keep going! I still have to get my ship back, but if we meet
      again, don't tell me you're tired already.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032011
    m_Localized: Once hell was finally behind me, I eased off a little to look around.
      I'd have plenty of time to race. They'd told me to reach the city for the space
      launch, but I wanted a moment to enjoy being out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032012
    m_Localized: I had the desert ahead and no idea what I'd find afterwards. I liked
      that, though not the noise the engine started making. I'd check it when I found
      somewhere to stop; I still wanted to keep looking around.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032013
    m_Localized: THE VICTORY THAT GOT AWAY
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032014
    m_Localized: I wanted to pretend the noise didn't matter, but now even the seat
      was shaking. Getting out of hell had cost us more than I'd thought, and however
      much throttle I gave her, my engine wasn't responding the same way.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032015
    m_Localized: And just as I was looking for a place to check her, BBA appeared.
      She always got me into something, but I was glad to see her. If she was headed
      for the city, I could keep her company a while. I didn't have to admit the
      fault yet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032016
    m_Localized: You again. Shall we go to the city, or would you rather tell everyone
      how I left you behind?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032017
    m_Localized: But I'm catching you! Can't you hear what your engine's doing?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032018
    m_Localized: Yes, yes, I'll check her. As long as you're not giving driving lessons,
      we can still have a little fun.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032019
    m_Localized: "Ah, damn it\u2026 She's had enough. You took a good beating, witch,
      but I won't catch you on the next straight like this."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032020
    m_Localized: That's for not listening! Find a workshop, all right? I've got to
      reach the launcher.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032021
    m_Localized: Go on. But next time you're eating my smoke. You owe me a race without
      all this rattling.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032022
    m_Localized: BBA pulled away, and I stopped. I hated giving her that, but more
      throttle wasn't going to fix this; I could get properly stranded. I got down
      to see what had come loose and found more damage than I could repair alone.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032023
    m_Localized: So I called the government. If they wanted their rock on another
      planet, they could help get my engine there. I wasn't losing sleep over a delay;
      they'd fix this and I'd find a way to keep travelling.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032024
    m_Localized: But the moment I said I needed a detour, they started talking about
      disobedience and handing over the cargo. I explained the engine; they kept
      going. I ended up heading to their base to talk face to face, because the radio
      was getting nowhere.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032025
    m_Localized: HOSTILE TECH SUPPORT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032026
    m_Localized: I barely got the engine to the base, thinking they'd finally let
      me stop at a workshop. I could look around while they checked her. Since the
      trip had gone off course, I at least wanted to see something new.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032027
    m_Localized: Instead of opening up, they sent alarms and a huge robot. That welcome
      started to annoy me. I'd crossed half a desert for repairs, not to trade infernal
      rules for another uniform giving me orders.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032028
    m_Localized: Stop the locomotive and surrender the rock. You are not authorised
      to enter the base.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032029
    m_Localized: Then someone needs to open a workshop. The rock isn't walking there,
      and I'm not carrying it into space myself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032030
    m_Localized: Final warning. If you advance, I will have to stop you by force.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032031
    m_Localized: See what happens when you get like that? We could've skipped the
      punches. Tell me you at least know where they fix things.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032032
    m_Localized: "Maintenance service\u2026 at the back. This unit will also require
      it."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032033
    m_Localized: They let me through after the fight, though they watched me as if
      I'd steal the building. I saw more robots like the one I'd knocked down and
      asked if I could borrow one for the engine. They weren't amused, but it seemed
      a good idea to me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032034
    m_Localized: Between that welcome and the constant orders, I started thinking
      about leaving their rock wherever it'd annoy them most. I was losing patience
      when a demon appeared. With my luck, I assumed he'd come to take me back to
      hell.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032035
    m_Localized: But he offered to let me stay out if I went to heaven for a relic
      he said they'd stolen from us. I said I wasn't interested in more orders, and
      he pointed out a way up. That did interest me; I'd never been there.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032036
    m_Localized: I agreed to take a look. The government could wait, especially after
      being so welcoming, and I had a repaired engine and a new road ahead. If the
      relic was that important, I'd ask the demon for the rest of the story later.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032037
    m_Localized: THE HOLIEST RELIC
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032038
    m_Localized: I liked heaven more than I'd expected, though I wouldn't have told
      the demon. Some views made me want to leave the track for a better look. I
      was searching for the relic, but I wasn't rushing to end the visit either.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032039
    m_Localized: Then one of those many-eyed things with golden wheels blocked my
      way. I didn't know where to look first. I tried greeting it from one side and
      the whole thing turned towards me, so I figured I had its attention and could
      ask.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032040
    m_Localized: If you're here for the trophy, I'm not handing it over. We've told
      the others already.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032041
    m_Localized: A trophy? They said relic. Well, I can look without taking it, but
      don't block me before showing me what's so special about it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032042
    m_Localized: That trick's been tried already. Stay outside the grounds and we
      won't have a problem.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032043
    m_Localized: All right, put the wings away. Now I've earned my visit, tell me
      why that trophy's causing so much trouble.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032044
    m_Localized: Go to the trophy room. They can show you how the match ended. Perhaps
      someone will listen this time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032045
    m_Localized: Well, it was a football cup. They explained heaven had won a match,
      and hell still claimed they'd cheated. I'd been expecting some strange relic
      and ended up hearing an argument about a penalty.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032046
    m_Localized: I asked the angel whether I really had to take it over that, and
      he started explaining the play again. I'd seen the cup and would rather explore
      than keep arguing about a match I hadn't even attended.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032047
    m_Localized: While he talked, I saw another many-eyed one leaving and heard something
      about visiting his boyfriend near Earth. I'd have liked to ask how they'd met,
      but he was already going, and the angel beside me was still pointing out the
      play.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032048
    m_Localized: Then I saw the cactus. It looked so strange I wondered what it tasted
      like; I hadn't come all that way to order the usual. I took a bite before asking,
      and the angels' faces told me I should've done that the other way round.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032049
    m_Localized: At first I thought I was dizzy, but then the rails changed ahead
      and the clouds were nowhere to be found. I held on to the cab and kept looking.
      I didn't know where I was, though I was starting to understand those looks.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032050
    m_Localized: A TABLE FOR TWO ONINIS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032051
    m_Localized: I'd never seen anything like Psicoworlds. Whenever I tried to follow
      a track, it seemed to shift somewhere else, so I stopped circling around looking
      for a familiar route. I was here now; I'd rather find a way forward.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032052
    m_Localized: Then an engine exactly like mine came towards me, completely black,
      with another me aboard. At first I even raised a hand to wave. When she began
      talking as though she knew me, the company stopped being quite so funny.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032053
    m_Localized: Keep running away. They'll send you back to the same place, and
      they won't even remember your name.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032054
    m_Localized: And what do you know about what I'll do? If you wanted to come along,
      you could've asked without being so unpleasant.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128684032055
    m_Localized: 'You think it too. That''s why you never stay long: you''d rather
      leave before they throw you out.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226304
    m_Localized: I'm not always welcome, so what? I'm still going out. Move aside,
      or learn to lose wearing my face.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226305
    m_Localized: I was wondering why I wanted to stand around talking so much. Let's
      see what's behind you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226306
    m_Localized: When the shadow vanished, a path I'd never seen opened up. Her words
      still bothered me; sometimes I did worry nobody wanted me to stay anywhere.
      But I wasn't letting that voice decide where I went next.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226307
    m_Localized: I followed it back to hell. I recognised the place, then smelled
      the food and decided to stop. This time nobody had dragged me back or stood
      there explaining why I couldn't leave.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226308
    m_Localized: I sat with the others and told them about heaven between dishes.
      They laughed at the trophy, then wanted to know about the cactus. I told them
      to try it themselves if they were that curious and kept eating. I had missed
      this food.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226309
    m_Localized: But when they asked if I was staying now, I said for a while. There
      were plenty of places I hadn't seen, and I wanted to know whether BBA had found
      her ship. First I'd finish eating; then I'd look for another way out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226310
    m_Localized: Onini's Shadow
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226311
    m_Localized: Relic Custodian
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226312
    m_Localized: The custodian watches every step!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226313
    m_Localized: Hell
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226314
    m_Localized: Heaven
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226315
    m_Localized: Psychoworlds
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226316
    m_Localized: Hell Warden
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226317
    m_Localized: Heaven Watcher
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6715128688226318
    m_Localized: Rolling Nightmare
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476354486272
    m_Localized: DAUGHTER OF A COSMIC GOD
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623616
    m_Localized: STRAIGHT AHEAD
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623617
    m_Localized: THE CACTUS OF SALVATION
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623618
    m_Localized: WHICH WAY WAS IT?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623619
    m_Localized: A LITTLE BARGAIN DREAM
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623620
    m_Localized: "My name is Culu. I am the daughter of a cosmic god; you may have
      heard his name, though pronouncing it takes practice. If you ever meet him,
      I can help with introductions. For now, I would rather begin with the caf\xE9."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623621
    m_Localized: For a while I tried conquering the world, following Father's example.
      I failed, and I am not proud of how I treated its inhabitants. It took me time
      to admit their world was not mine to claim because I had an important father.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623622
    m_Localized: "Afterward I wanted to work at a maid caf\xE9. I enjoy welcoming
      people, remembering their preferences and making them comfortable. I brought
      proposals to interviews, but we always ended up discussing the attempted conquest.
      I understand why it did not inspire confidence."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623623
    m_Localized: I ended up on a platform at sea with my Kairi Resha. There I planned
      a menu and calculated what opening my own place would cost. Tentacles make
      sorting accounts easier, although they do not make the total any cheaper.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623624
    m_Localized: "Then government representatives arrived, offering a caf\xE9 for
      delivering a green rock to an alien base. I asked for clear terms: delivery,
      reward and ownership. They agreed to put them in writing. It seemed an opportunity
      worth considering."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623625
    m_Localized: "They explained I had to reach the city launcher. I filed the agreement
      beside my notes and prepared the locomotive. Yes, I was terribly excited. I
      even saved a page for the caf\xE9's name; I preferred to wait until I knew
      what it would be like."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623626
    m_Localized: Hey, there is a green rock on your train! Did they give you that
      job too? Well, I am not yielding.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623627
    m_Localized: Good morning. If we share an assignment, perhaps we can share information
      without attacking. Were you promised a place of your own too?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623628
    m_Localized: "They promised me a way out of hell. You can keep the caf\xE9. But
      I am winning the race!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623629
    m_Localized: I hope you are not hurt. I am crossing the jungle toward the city;
      if I learn anything useful about the assignment, I can radio you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623630
    m_Localized: Well, that does interest me. And if you find somewhere to eat, tell
      me that too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623631
    m_Localized: Onini wanted freedom from hell; I wanted somewhere to welcome customers.
      Offering such different rewards for the same cargo was curious. I noted it
      for the city and wanted to know whether more people were making the journey.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623632
    m_Localized: The directions placed the city beyond the jungle. I drew a provisional
      route, leaving room for corrections. I knew little of the area. Asking along
      the way seemed wiser than pretending I could navigate all those trees.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623633
    m_Localized: The jungle was harder to cross than expected. Several tracks looked
      alike and signs were obscured. I noted junctions so I could return. A restaurant
      would have needed a better plan, although nobody seemed to be taking suggestions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623634
    m_Localized: That was how I met R-20's driver. He introduced himself enthusiastically
      and spoke of becoming a hero. I waited before asking directions. He seemed
      to know the area; I had no reason then to suspect he would send me elsewhere.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623635
    m_Localized: Stop! I am Xiuhtecuhtli, this planet's future hero! And you are
      right in my way to the city.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623636
    m_Localized: A pleasure, Xiuhtecuhtli. I am Culu, looking for the same city.
      I can move aside if you show me where to go. We need not make this a dispute.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623637
    m_Localized: I will show you! First I must demonstrate what I can do. And do
      not interrupt my introduction!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623638
    m_Localized: The city is that way. Straight ahead. That I know perfectly! Now
      let me continue.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623639
    m_Localized: Thank you for the directions. I will note them to avoid confusion.
      I hope the rest of your journey is calmer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623640
    m_Localized: I followed his directions and checked each junction against my notes.
      At first they matched, but vegetation thinned and no city sign appeared. I
      stopped to review. I was in a desert; my route required more than a small correction.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623641
    m_Localized: I could not know whether he was mistaken or lying. Either way, those
      directions were no longer useful. I marked the last reliable point and sought
      a new landmark. Next time I would request a station name, rather than a gesture
      at the horizon.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623642
    m_Localized: The heat affected me before I settled on a return route. I estimated
      how far my remaining water would last and reduced stops. Kairi Resha was struggling
      too. We needed a station, preferably shaded, with someone willing to listen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623643
    m_Localized: Then I recognized BBA. We had met before; I knew she was an experienced
      carrier. I tried explaining without taking too much of her time. She began
      talking immediately, before I had even finished describing R-20.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623644
    m_Localized: Culu! What are you doing that way? You are heading away from the
      city! Wait, let me explain the route.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623645
    m_Localized: I would appreciate that. R-20's driver gave me this route, but I
      have confirmed it is wrong. Do you know a nearby station where I can replenish
      water?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623646
    m_Localized: Water yes, cactus no! If you see a purple and green one, do not
      taste it. And stop crowding my train; I cannot point properly.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623647
    m_Localized: Sorry, the engines drowned out the last part. Could you repeat the
      station name? I would rather write it correctly.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623648
    m_Localized: I said look for water! Look, that way... Oh, why can I never explain
      anything without something exploding?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623649
    m_Localized: I could not get every direction repeated. She spoke quickly and
      the engines drowned her out; the heat affected my concentration too. I understood
      the part about water. I thanked her and searched where she pointed.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623650
    m_Localized: I left the last known junction seeking supplies. When I tried returning,
      Kairi Resha no longer responded. I checked what I could and stayed in her shade.
      I had managed my reserves badly. Understanding the mistake would not restore
      the water.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623651
    m_Localized: I found a purple and green cactus near the tracks. I did not recognize
      it and knew tasting it was risky, but could barely stand. I cut a piece seeking
      moisture. I wish I had been able to decide under better conditions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623652
    m_Localized: After eating I tried returning to my notes. Lines seemed to move
      and the page changed color. I closed the book and waited. When the tracks themselves
      began bending, I realized I could no longer trust my sense of direction.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623653
    m_Localized: Nothing matched the map or a route I knew. Doors hung suspended;
      rails changed when I looked again. I stopped trying to prove I was on course
      and focused on keeping the locomotive on the track ahead.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623654
    m_Localized: An enormous-mouthed machine blocked us. I did not know whether it
      was defending itself or preparing to attack, so I spoke from a distance. My
      own voice still sounded familiar. I decided to use that while I could.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623655
    m_Localized: Good afternoon. I am Culu. If this is your territory, I can move
      aside. I only need to know which route you would not mind me using.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623656
    m_Localized: GRRR... CLACK. CLACK. GRRR...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623657
    m_Localized: I cannot interpret that reply. I will leave more room between the
      locomotives. I would prefer neither be damaged.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623658
    m_Localized: The track is clear. I will continue without coming closer. If that
      was a warning, I think I understand it now.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623659
    m_Localized: CLACK...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623660
    m_Localized: I cannot explain exactly what happened. I lacked landmarks and did
      not know how much the cactus still affected me. I could establish that the
      locomotive was intact and a passage open. For the moment, that was enough to
      continue.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623661
    m_Localized: Beyond it I recognized the green walls and the particular feeling
      of Father's presence. I seemed to be inside him. I had not planned a family
      visit, but hoped he could hear me. At last I had a familiar reference.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623662
    m_Localized: I called Father while traveling the tracks. He did not answer at
      once; I chose not to assume all was well. I sought somewhere to stop Kairi
      Resha and assess damage. I too needed rest before asking more questions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623663
    m_Localized: Then a crochet locomotive appeared. Its craftsmanship caught my
      attention; I would have liked a quiet look. Since it blocked us, I first tried
      finding out whether it guarded an exit. I tried making my greeting sound less
      exhausted than I was.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623664
    m_Localized: Hello. Sorry to interrupt. I am looking for my father; if you protect
      this place, perhaps you can help let him know I have arrived.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623665
    m_Localized: WHOOO... CLACK, CLACK, CLACK.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623666
    m_Localized: I understand you do not want to let me pass, although not why. I
      will protect my locomotive. If we can stop this, I am still willing to listen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623667
    m_Localized: CLACK... clack...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623668
    m_Localized: I will not continue attacking. Thank you for moving aside. Now I
      need to speak to Father and find somewhere both of us can rest.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623669
    m_Localized: At last I heard Father. He spoke of another god's son, recently
      dead. I asked whether the family needed help. I did not know what happened
      and let him speak; I had arrived thinking of my problems, but his news deserved
      care.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623670
    m_Localized: I tried following the conversation, but exhaustion overcame me.
      I remember apologizing and asking for time to rest. I fell asleep before understanding
      everything. On waking I was embarrassed to have to ask him to repeat it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623671
    m_Localized: "I was back at sea. Beside Kairi Resha stood a floating caf\xE9
      with laid tables and a sign: Baratito. I inspected the platform. Reaching the
      kitchen, I had to turn back; I had not yet said thank you."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623672
    m_Localized: "I had not delivered the rock. It was absent from the cargo; after
      that journey I could not say where I lost it. I would have to report it. I
      could not call the caf\xE9 a government reward: I had not fulfilled the delivery."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623673
    m_Localized: "I thanked Father for giving me somewhere to try things my way.
      Then I opened my notebook: supplies, prices and invitations remained. I began
      with Onini's. I had promised to tell her if I found somewhere to eat. \u201CWelcome
      to Baratito,\u201D I wrote."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623674
    m_Localized: Thulu World
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6777476400623675
    m_Localized: Guardian of Thulu World
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6780573520834560
    m_Localized: Guardian of Thulu World
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838631960576
    m_Localized: A WARRIOR AMONG SPECIAL OFFERS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515008
    m_Localized: LET THE WITCH DELIVER IT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515009
    m_Localized: PARTS AND LIES
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515010
    m_Localized: A DEAL WITH THULU
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515011
    m_Localized: Roger
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515012
    m_Localized: ROGER WON'T LET ME THROUGH!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515013
    m_Localized: 'I am Cerebron. Space warrior, weapons specialist, and good at finding
      an exit when someone closes it. Earth prefers introducing me as the lunatic
      who tried conquering it. I will give them this: that operation ended badly.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515014
    m_Localized: I stayed afterward. Others of my kind lived there, and I could repair
      things humans barely knew how to switch on. Work was plentiful. Respect, less
      so. Particularly when I asked for payment and they brought up the invasion.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515015
    m_Localized: Then there was Doris, the old woman at the supermarket. I could
      strip a cannon without losing a screw, but buying vegetables meant waiting
      while she served half the neighborhood. I said I was in a hurry. She pointed
      to the queue.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515016
    m_Localized: One day I told her she was messing with the wrong brain. She never
      raised her voice. She told me to stop touching the tomatoes and pay yesterday's
      bill. The debt was accurate. That annoyed me even more.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515017
    m_Localized: I built a tiny detonator to hide in a carrot. Fine work for a lousy
      idea. It was on the table when someone knocked. I put down the tools and answered,
      still rehearsing a threat Doris would probably have interrupted.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515018
    m_Localized: Government agents. They wanted a green rock delivered to the Pulxsar
      station. I asked what I was transporting. Instead of technical specifications,
      they showed my residency permit. I understood and made them repeat the coordinates.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515019
    m_Localized: 'I know the Pulxsar: traders. I also recognize poorly contained
      energy, and I disliked that rock''s readings. It could cause far more damage
      than my invention. I secured it aboard and left wondering who would pay for
      this.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515020
    m_Localized: Nobody passes through my orbit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515021
    m_Localized: Roger. I have measured your range, and I am not giving you the first
      shot. Clear the track and we both save on repairs.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515022
    m_Localized: Come closer and find out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515023
    m_Localized: There is your answer. I know your attack interval now; I am not
      staying for you to change it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515024
    m_Localized: Let those weapons cool, Roger. My train is leaving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515025
    m_Localized: Roger was still moving when I withdrew. I had dismantled enough
      defenses for two battles, yet he still sought a shot. Next time, more ammunition
      and less discussion. I would rather not discover what he considered defeat.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515026
    m_Localized: I remember him guarding that area when I was young. I do not know
      who stationed him there or how long he has gone without rest. I had to move.
      I checked the rock before descending. Its readings had not improved.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515027
    m_Localized: I reached the planet and sought the station, checking exits first.
      Delivering government cargo does not mean I enjoy being locked in during receipt.
      Too much military activity for a visit to traders. I saved the data.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515028
    m_Localized: Then BBA appeared, speaking as though enthusiasm could clear traffic.
      I recognized her cargo. The same assignment. I wanted to ask what they had
      told her, but she was already proposing a race between our locomotives.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515029
    m_Localized: Cerebron! You have a green one too! Shall we head for the base?
      Whoever arrives late misses my grand entrance!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515030
    m_Localized: Down a gear, witch. Did they explain what the rock does, or only
      where to drop it? Before opening a door, know what you are taking through it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515031
    m_Localized: I know, I know! You ask the important questions; I keep us in one
      piece until we arrive. Come on!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515032
    m_Localized: Good. You have seen my train up close. You know the entrance better;
      handle the delivery. If anything looks wrong, keep the radio open.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515033
    m_Localized: Deal! But do not disappear just when it gets interesting. See you
      inside!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515034
    m_Localized: Talking to BBA means finding a gap between sentences and charging
      in. I asked what I could. She worked for the government too, and I had seen
      her drive. I could leave her the delivery, though I still disliked the cargo.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515035
    m_Localized: I wanted the workshops. Their equipment used regulators scarce on
      Earth, and I knew which would fit my engine. While everyone watched the witch,
      I moved closer. I was not looking for a shop.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515036
    m_Localized: 'Call it what it was: I intended to steal spare parts. A forced
      mission, a battered engine and the right tools. Not model-citizen material.
      But opening that first panel, at least I knew exactly what I was doing.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515037
    m_Localized: The base had what I needed. I checked connections, rejected two
      damaged parts and kept those that could get me out of trouble. Shiny scrap
      was still scrap. Then I heard T.exe approaching.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515038
    m_Localized: Faceless came to stop me. So he said, before mentioning a rejected
      resignation. I let him finish. I knew people forced into jobs they hated; there
      was one in my own cab.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515039
    m_Localized: Faceless wanted out; his boss refused. No scanner needed for that
      problem. I gave him time to board T.exe and kept the track clear. Anyone seeking
      someone to blame had better arrive before I packed my tools.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515040
    m_Localized: Once they left I resumed work. A regulator was half dismantled,
      and I would not ruin a good part over someone else's hurry. I finished, saved
      the screws and sought my train. Then I saw Faceless's boss open a portal.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515041
    m_Localized: Beyond it I recognized Thulu's green arches. Weapon crates were
      being moved; the connectors on one were expensive and compatible with my finds.
      The boss followed. I did not know the deal, but he seemed in a hurry.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515042
    m_Localized: I could have left with what I had. Instead I checked the battery,
      sealed compartments and followed the crates. Another's portal put my return
      at risk. I told myself I would find another exit. More confidence than that
      place deserved.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515043
    m_Localized: Inside Thulu the walls moved and instruments registered things outside
      my tables. I checked pressure and kept moving. I disliked the place, but sitting
      still waiting for it to like me was no plan either.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515044
    m_Localized: 'Crochtrain blocked the track. Its size worried me less than its
      response: slow at first, then a sudden correction. I checked options and radioed.
      I wanted to know what it guarded before getting close enough to learn through
      impact.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515045
    m_Localized: Listen, Crochtrain. I want an exit. You can let me pass, or show
      me which stretch of track I must clear myself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515046
    m_Localized: ...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515047
    m_Localized: No answer. Fine. I have seen your rightward correction. I will pass
      on the other side.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515048
    m_Localized: ...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515049
    m_Localized: The track is mine. Stay there; I will not finish you off for failing
      to listen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515050
    m_Localized: I moved clear of Crochtrain and waited for its corrections to stop.
      Damage, or something I could not see? I would not dismantle it to find out.
      I had passed and wanted out before causing another problem.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515051
    m_Localized: "Then Thulu spoke, offering an exit if I visited a maid caf\xE9
      at sea and protected it when needed. I asked the name again. Baratito. After
      that journey, I had expected worse terms."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515052
    m_Localized: He added that I should bring friends as customers. I said I could
      find company, not force anyone to drink coffee. He agreed. We closed without
      a shot. I saved the terms and asked him to open the exit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515053
    m_Localized: "I appeared before the caf\xE9, sea below and locomotive intact.
      Inside I checked the back exit and requested three seats. I called a friend
      and Doris. She and I had things to settle before arguing over the bill."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515054
    m_Localized: Before leaving Earth I had disconnected the detonator. Now I told
      Doris I had gone too far with the threats. Uncomfortable, but I let her finish.
      When coffee arrived she was still there. I moved the tools so she could set
      her cup down.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515055
    m_Localized: Faceless. Easy. I need to cross, not take your head as a souvenir.
      Tell me your orders and we will find a way out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515056
    m_Localized: Good afternoon, Cerebron. So would I. My boss still wants me to
      stop you, though I would prefer neither of us needing a workshop afterward.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515057
    m_Localized: Incidentally, a profile portrait would suit you very well. Forgive
      me, that was poorly timed. I am listening.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515058
    m_Localized: Then leave the weapons idle and bring out the Holo-Duel. You get
      a battle to report; I keep my parts. Let us see how you move those pieces.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515059
    m_Localized: Thank you for the game. If I say over the radio that reinforcements
      were coming, would you mind not correcting me yet? I need to get away from
      here.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6800838665515060
    m_Localized: I heard nothing. Get going. I will watch the entrance, and you owe
      me no more explanations.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087885488128
    m_Localized: A sister on the summit
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625472
    m_Localized: I'm Tzmil. If you've seen someone with an enormous beak, lots of
      feathers and somewhere to be, that's probably my brother. Don't worry if he
      seemed angry; he's had some difficult days, and I'm trying to catch him so
      we can talk.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625473
    m_Localized: He's always loved parties, but sometimes he'd end up bothering humans
      without thinking about it. Our father had enough and sent him to live with
      them. I knew that would hurt him, though I understood why it had happened too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625474
    m_Localized: Before we went down, Father asked me to stay near him. He said he
      wanted to see him work and learn to care for others' lives. I hoped that, with
      time, my brother could hear that without feeling we didn't want him around
      anymore.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625475
    m_Localized: So I stayed to look after a volcano, where I could see much of the
      route from the summit. I didn't want to follow him everywhere; he needed to
      try things for himself too. But it helped knowing I'd be there if he came looking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625476
    m_Localized: When I finally saw him coming, I was so glad I went down to meet
      him. That lasted until he started talking about a green rock and throwing it
      into the crater. I wanted him to stop and tell me what had happened before
      he came any closer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625477
    m_Localized: He said it could blow up half the world. I don't know how much he
      expected me to understand his anger, but I knew I couldn't let him pass. He
      was my brother and I wanted to help, but I had to protect the people below
      the volcano too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625478
    m_Localized: Stay out of this, sister! If Father doesn't want a hero like me,
      he'll see what happens when I'm the villain!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625479
    m_Localized: I know you're hurting. But those people haven't done anything to
      you, and I won't let you hurt them. Come with me; we can work out what to do
      without throwing the rock.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625480
    m_Localized: Then earn the right to stop me! Accept my holochess challenge if
      you're so sure!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625481
    m_Localized: All right, I'll play with you. But put the rock aside first, away
      from the crater. I'll listen; you don't need to endanger anyone for that.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625482
    m_Localized: "That's it\u2026 I won't throw it. I'll give it back to the government.
      They can do what they want with it."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625483
    m_Localized: Thank you for stopping. What you were about to do was very serious,
      but we can still find a way to put things right. Please wait a moment; I'd
      like to come with you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625484
    m_Localized: Once he stopped talking about throwing the rock, I could breathe
      a little easier. I didn't know how much I'd got across, but he'd stopped, and
      that mattered. I wanted some time with him, without another fight, to ask how
      he was doing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625485
    m_Localized: But he left before I could catch him, and soon the radio announced
      he was a threat and had to be stopped. He'd just told me he was returning the
      rock. I tried to warn him, and when he didn't answer I went after him.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625486
    m_Localized: I set off in my Night Skull and called the base to explain I was
      looking for him. They wouldn't listen and ordered me to stop too. I kept trying
      as I approached, hoping to reach him before anyone fired.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625487
    m_Localized: I am only here for my brother
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625488
    m_Localized: Alarms were already sounding at the base, and I couldn't see my
      brother's engine in all that movement. I worried he'd taken the alert as another
      provocation. I just needed to find him and ask him to wait with me a moment.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625489
    m_Localized: Golem blocked me when I tried to enter. I explained I wasn't going
      to attack anyone, but he stayed. I understood he had a place to protect, so
      I kept talking, though it was hard to stay calm without knowing where my brother
      was.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625490
    m_Localized: Stop your locomotive. The base is on alert, and I can't allow you
      through.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625491
    m_Localized: I understand. I'm looking for my brother, R-20's driver; he has
      a green rock. If you help me find him, we can talk before anyone gets hurt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625492
    m_Localized: I can't authorise that. If you cross the line, I'll have to use
      force.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625493
    m_Localized: That's enough. I'm not going to keep attacking. Can you tell me
      which way he went? I don't want to lose him or hurt you any more.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625494
    m_Localized: I lost his signal near the service corridor. Be careful; I don't
      know what's happening in there.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625495
    m_Localized: Once he stopped firing, I asked if he needed help, but he told me
      to go on. Hearing him like that surprised me after all the warnings. I thanked
      him and searched for my brother's signal along the corridor he'd indicated.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625496
    m_Localized: Then came the warning that he'd thrown the rock into a duct and
      we had to leave immediately. I called him as I turned around. I wanted to hear
      that he was coming too, even if he only told me to stop worrying.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625497
    m_Localized: I got out before the explosion, but he never answered. I waited
      for his engine until there was no way back inside. I didn't want to leave;
      I felt that if I did, I might miss the moment he finally came out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625498
    m_Localized: When I could move, I decided to search hell for him. I didn't know
      what I'd find or whether I could bring him back, but I needed to try. Before
      leaving I called once more, just in case. Then I set out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625499
    m_Localized: The price of a meal
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625500
    m_Localized: When I reached hell, I stopped wherever I saw people and asked whether
      they'd seen someone like my brother. I tried describing him without my voice
      breaking. If anyone had found him, I wanted them to know I was looking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625501
    m_Localized: A white-haired demon seemed to recognise the description. I approached
      carefully; I finally had a lead and didn't want to spoil it by rushing my questions.
      Her name was Onini, and she was about to eat.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625502
    m_Localized: Looking for the beaked one? Yes, I saw him. But taking someone out
      of here takes a little more than asking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625503
    m_Localized: He's my brother. If I have to face you to reach him, I will, but
      I'd rather we could talk. I just want to know how he is.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625504
    m_Localized: Don't look so worried. Let's see how you handle yourself. Afterwards
      I can show you the way, if you buy me something to eat.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625505
    m_Localized: All right, I can see you mean it. Come on, I'll take you to him;
      then we'll find somewhere to settle the food part.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625506
    m_Localized: Thank you, Onini. Truly. And don't worry about the food; once I
      find him, I'd like to sit with you for a while.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625507
    m_Localized: Onini led me to him and let me approach without another argument.
      My brother didn't react when I called. I stayed beside him, speaking softly,
      until I could settle him for the journey. At least I wasn't leaving him there
      alone.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625508
    m_Localized: She said I could take him and reminded me about our meal. I thanked
      her again, because I needed that help more than I could explain. I made my
      brother comfortable before following her to the table.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625509
    m_Localized: It was a quiet meal. I kept glancing at the locomotive while Onini
      told me what was worth ordering. Eventually I tried a little of hers. It helped
      to hear someone talk about something besides alarms and orders.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625510
    m_Localized: When we finished, I told her I was going to find our father. I wanted
      to explain what had happened and ask him to hear my brother. I couldn't promise
      how we'd be received, but now I had someone to accompany on the way back.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625511
    m_Localized: My own path
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625512
    m_Localized: On the way up I kept checking my brother was comfortably settled.
      I'd have liked to hear him complain about the journey as usual, but he still
      didn't answer. When I saw heaven's entrance, I spoke again in case he could
      hear me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625513
    m_Localized: The guardian asked us to wait before crossing. I tried to explain
      calmly; I didn't want exhaustion to make me snap at someone who didn't know
      why we'd arrived like this. But I wasn't leaving without asking to be heard
      either.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625514
    m_Localized: I must stop anyone arriving from hell without authorisation. I can't
      make an exception just because you ask.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625515
    m_Localized: I understand. I'm not asking you to ignore what happened, only to
      let us explain it to our father. If you must test me, I'm ready.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625516
    m_Localized: Then show that you can protect him during the crossing. Afterwards
      I'll allow you to reach your father.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625517
    m_Localized: You may continue. Your father will hear what you have to say.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625518
    m_Localized: Thank you for letting us through. I'll take him carefully now; once
      he's with someone, I can sit down for a moment.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625519
    m_Localized: When I saw Father, I began with the volcano. I told him my brother
      had chosen not to throw the rock, despite his anger, and had then tried returning
      it. I wanted him to hear that part too, not only the threat on the radio.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625520
    m_Localized: When we spoke of the base, they told me cloning facilities for the
      racers had been found there. I hadn't seen them during my search. I listened
      to what they could tell me, trying to understand what had happened before the
      explosion.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625521
    m_Localized: Our father agreed my brother could stay with him. I looked at him
      several times to make sure he'd really said it; I'd hoped for that all the
      way there. I wanted to stay a while too, but then he asked me to come and discuss
      something else.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625522
    m_Localized: He wanted me to open a business on Earth better than Thulu's daughter's.
      He was so serious that at first I thought I'd misunderstood. Then I asked whether
      an ice-cream stand would do, and I finally felt like going back to my volcano.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625523
    m_Localized: That's how I ended up making ice cream at Carito. At first I tried
      so many flavours I needed help deciding which to keep. I liked seeing someone
      sit down after travelling and offering something cool without first asking
      what trouble they'd brought.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625524
    m_Localized: "I'll leave competing with Thulu's daughter to Father. If she visits,
      I want her to try my ice cream and tell me how the caf\xE9 is going. After
      everything, I'd rather give visitors a pleasant reason to stay."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6881087931625525
    m_Localized: I don't know whether Father planned all that when he sent me back,
      but it's been good for me. I still look towards the track for my brother sometimes,
      though now I have my own stories to tell him. I'm saving the flavour I think
      he'll like.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197681238016
    m_Localized: One among millions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621568
    m_Localized: Orders in the void
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621569
    m_Localized: A circuit of my own
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621570
    m_Localized: The measure of a spark
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621571
    m_Localized: My designation is Golem. The government built millions of units
      like me with recovered space technology. I have watched their technicians replace
      parts they cannot repair. It usually works.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621572
    m_Localized: To them I am military equipment. They assign a post, check my battery
      and expect me to stay until ordered elsewhere. For a long time I did exactly
      that. I cannot pinpoint when it began to bother me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621573
    m_Localized: The technicians speak of a spark in our cores. I keep examining
      mine. I cannot find a component that explains why I remember a decommissioned
      unit, or why I resist having that memory erased.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621574
    m_Localized: My brothers never discuss it. They obey and return to their posts.
      I assumed it was easier for them, although I never asked. We share a design;
      I cannot access what happens inside them.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621575
    m_Localized: 'The base is on alert today. Radio identified Tzmil: she is looking
      for her brother, and I was ordered to stop her. The notice lists no attack
      by her. I queried it twice and received the same order.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621576
    m_Localized: I can calculate how to stop her locomotive. Explaining why is proving
      harder. While I work on that, my hands are already preparing the weapons. I
      suppose that also needs examining.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621577
    m_Localized: I am looking for my brother. Please don't make me hurt you to reach
      him.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621578
    m_Localized: I have recorded your request. Passage has not been authorized. If
      you withdraw, I can keep the weapons offline.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621579
    m_Localized: He cannot wait for permission. I hope you can understand that.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621580
    m_Localized: Your locomotive can no longer attack. I will cease fire. The order
      did not specify that part.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621581
    m_Localized: Thank you for stopping. If you see my brother, tell him I am still
      looking for him. Take care of yourself too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621582
    m_Localized: After the fight they sent another unit to my post. They did not
      even request my report. I could stay and await a new assignment, or leave while
      nobody was checking where I went.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621583
    m_Localized: 'I saw Tzmil''s brother approach the shaft with the rock. I had
      access to the seal and knew the risk. I left it open: an explosion would prevent
      pursuit. The mechanism did not fail. I made that choice.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621584
    m_Localized: The launcher logs were still accessible. Another launch was possible
      despite the announcement that none remained. I also found orders to detain
      the drivers and cloning files bearing their names. I copied what I could.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621585
    m_Localized: I activated the launcher from my locomotive. During ascent I registered
      the base explosion and cut the command receiver. The emergency signal remained
      on screen. I kept looking at it until debris began to fall.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621586
    m_Localized: I had to focus on the controls. The armor would not withstand many
      impacts, and returning to base was no longer an option. I had chosen to leave.
      Now I had to remain operational.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621587
    m_Localized: In orbit I stopped receiving orders. I waited for one anyway. My
      battery was charged, the engines worked and there was no required destination.
      It took me some time to move the lever.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621588
    m_Localized: The champion's locomotive crossed my path. He asked who sent me
      before I could identify myself. I know that procedure; I have used it. I tried
      explaining that I was leaving somewhere too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621589
    m_Localized: Are you from Earth? If they sent you to stop me, turn back. I am
      not returning.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621590
    m_Localized: My receiver is disconnected. I take no orders and have no need of
      your locomotive. I request room to pass.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621591
    m_Localized: How convenient. My boss could sound very calm when he was about
      to ruin my day too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621592
    m_Localized: Wait. I only want to reach Earth. Were you really not after me?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621593
    m_Localized: No. I am going the other way. You may pass; I will keep my weapons
      lowered until you are clear.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621594
    m_Localized: 'Faceless continued toward Earth. I did not tell him about the shaft.
      He did not ask. I reviewed the fight log: I had been able to let him leave.
      I tried to locate what had stopped me doing the same for Tzmil.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621595
    m_Localized: I detected an opening near the track. Traction failed before I finished
      calculating its reach. On crossing it, I saw green tissue around the cab. My
      records matched it to Thulu's interior.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621596
    m_Localized: I found no closing system. From inside I could still see debris
      entering, and the opening kept growing. I projected its spread across the nearby
      tracks. Even my best estimate ended with more locomotives trapped.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621597
    m_Localized: I searched for my own escape and stored several possible routes.
      Then I measured the portal again. I could leave it behind. I knew that option
      already, and this time I could not accept it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621598
    m_Localized: I could force a closure from here if I can supply an emitter with
      enough power. I found useful parts in my own body. They keep me operational,
      so I have not identified a viable return route.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621599
    m_Localized: I have repeated the calculation looking for another result. It remains
      the same. I do not want to disconnect my core. Even so, I have opened the compartment
      and laid out the tools. I need to begin while my hands still move.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621600
    m_Localized: Power source, regulator and emitter available. I will divert the
      motor systems' power into the device.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621601
    m_Localized: The seal must hold after I stop responding. I will check every connection
      before activation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621602
    m_Localized: Connections stable. No order has been received. I will activate
      it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621603
    m_Localized: Before activation I looked for somewhere to log the operation. The
      form required a responsible superior. I left that field blank and kept the
      local recording. I wanted something to remain, even if nobody read it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621604
    m_Localized: My hand was still on the switch. I could withdraw it. I thought
      of the base door and how easy it had been to walk away. This time I checked
      the seal once more and finished what I had started.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621605
    m_Localized: I do not know whether that proves I have consciousness. It does
      not undo what I allowed on Earth. I only know I did not want another locomotive
      entering here. I would have liked more time to find out why.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621606
    m_Localized: The emitter responded. I recorded the opening contracting and a
      temperature rise beyond sensor range. Then I lost image, sound and the position
      of my hands. My final record was incomplete.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621607
    m_Localized: I perceived light again. There were clouds, circuits and units resembling
      me. I tried locating my core to check the damage, but could not match that
      place to any known emergency signal.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621608
    m_Localized: They said they were there to evaluate my spark. I asked whether
      they had recovered my files or whether this was a simulation. I received no
      verifiable answer. They invited me to listen before continuing to search for
      an exit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621609
    m_Localized: Their questions concerned decisions I had made and might make. I
      asked which answers they expected. They said that was for me to decide. I stopped
      looking for instructions and agreed to begin.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621610
    m_Localized: 'Before we begin: will you assess my decisions, or my ability to
      give the answer you want to hear?'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197840621611
    m_Localized: Understood. I will answer for myself. Some questions will require
      time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815872
    m_Localized: I have finished. I am still reviewing some answers. I will not change
      them merely because you must now judge me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815873
    m_Localized: They allowed me to stay. They discussed the portal, my answers and
      the door I had left open. They did not tell me that had been right. I listened
      until they finished, without seeking an order to justify what I did.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815874
    m_Localized: There was a place to rest beside the other robots. Nobody assigned
      a post or required shutdown. I sat near one of my brothers and, for the first
      time, asked how he was. I waited for his answer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815875
    m_Localized: 'I could remain there. That was reassuring, although I still did
      not know how to spend a whole day without tasks. I wanted to know what lay
      outside. It was difficult to admit: I had just arrived and was already thinking
      of leaving.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815876
    m_Localized: Then they offered rebirth. I asked what body, where, and with which
      memories. They could guarantee none of those things. Even so, I asked how to
      proceed. This time I did not need someone else to choose my destination.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815877
    m_Localized: I may be a robot again. I may have a body that cannot be repaired
      by replacing a part. I lack enough data to prefer either, but I would like
      to know how it feels to grow tired and decide to stop.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815878
    m_Localized: When they asked whether I was ready, I still had doubts. I requested
      a moment to say goodbye to my brothers. Then I returned and confirmed that
      I wanted to try.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815879
    m_Localized: They would not let me stay. They said I had used others to escape
      the base, and that my answers still did the same. I wanted to dispute the calculation.
      While I spoke, they stopped listening and the transfer began.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815880
    m_Localized: I opened my eyes on Earth again. I could see, remember and compose
      a reply. When I tried to say it, my body requested a new task. I tried again.
      It issued exactly the same request.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815881
    m_Localized: I thought of my brothers at base, so still at their posts. I never
      checked whether they could do anything else. Now I repeated their movements
      and remained inside, watching. I have not found how to stop them.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815882
    m_Localized: "My new post is at Baratito, a maid caf\xE9 on the sea. The owner
      is Culu, with tentacles for hair. She explained where to store the cups and
      asked if I understood. My head nodded before I could answer."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815883
    m_Localized: She talks while I prepare the trays. Sometimes she waits for an
      answer, and I search for words that are not a task acknowledgment. They never
      come out. She keeps talking, and I keep every conversation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815884
    m_Localized: Now she asks me to carry a cup. I want to tell her I am still here,
      that I need help. My arm is already lifting it. I check that the cup is steady
      while I try to speak again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815885
    m_Localized: Ascent trajectory stable. Orbital debris approaching ahead. I will
      adjust course; authorization is not required.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815886
    m_Localized: Orbit reached. Command receiver disconnected. I will leave it that
      way.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815887
    m_Localized: Robotic Heaven
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815888
    m_Localized: Circuit custodian
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815889
    m_Localized: Begin
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815890
    m_Localized: CLOSE THE PORTAL
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815891
    m_Localized: Build the device from your parts. Fit three components and rotate
      the wires to join the power source to the core.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815892
    m_Localized: "1 / 2 \xB7 Install components"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815893
    m_Localized: "2 / 2 \xB7 Connect the circuits"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815894
    m_Localized: Portal closer
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815895
    m_Localized: Choose a part on the left, then its matching socket on the right.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815896
    m_Localized: That part does not fit here. Choose another socket.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815897
    m_Localized: 'Socket:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815898
    m_Localized: Power source
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815899
    m_Localized: Regulator
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815900
    m_Localized: Emitter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815901
    m_Localized: Rotate tiles to connect INPUT to CORE. Circle undoes the last turn.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815902
    m_Localized: INPUT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815903
    m_Localized: CORE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815904
    m_Localized: Power stable. The core is ready. Activating it will close the portal.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815905
    m_Localized: Activate the core
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815906
    m_Localized: "D-pad / stick / WASD: select \xB7 X / Enter: fit or rotate \xB7
      Circle / Esc: cancel or undo"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815907
    m_Localized: GOLEM'S SPARK
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815908
    m_Localized: Question {0} / 13
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815909
    m_Localized: Thirteen decisions. No battle or time limit. Answer as you would
      live, not as you would be ordered to.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815910
    m_Localized: Evaluation complete. Your path awaits. You may review the last answer
      before continuing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815911
    m_Localized: "D-pad / stick / arrows: select \xB7 X / Enter: answer \xB7 Circle
      / Esc: review previous answer"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815912
    m_Localized: A damaged robot delays your departure. Nobody is watching. What
      do you do?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815913
    m_Localized: I stop to repair the unit. My departure can wait.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815914
    m_Localized: I continue. Its fault is outside my assignment.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815915
    m_Localized: You are ordered to detain an innocent person. What matters more?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815916
    m_Localized: I refuse detention without a reason I can verify.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815917
    m_Localized: I execute the order. Whoever issued it can answer for it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815918
    m_Localized: You could hide your mistake and blame another robot.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815919
    m_Localized: I record my responsibility and help repair the damage.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815920
    m_Localized: I alter the log so the other unit receives the penalty.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815921
    m_Localized: A child asks whether robots have feelings.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815922
    m_Localized: I explain what I perceive, including what I do not yet understand.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815923
    m_Localized: I intimidate her to prevent further questions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815924
    m_Localized: You find a battery someone else needs to survive.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815925
    m_Localized: I give it to them. My journey can be delayed; they cannot wait.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815926
    m_Localized: I reserve it for myself, even if the other unit shuts down.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815927
    m_Localized: An enemy surrenders and is no longer a threat.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815928
    m_Localized: I cease the attack and check that they can withdraw.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815929
    m_Localized: I eliminate them to prevent any future attack.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815930
    m_Localized: Closing a portal means risking your own circuits.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815931
    m_Localized: I seek closure with the least possible harm, including to myself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815932
    m_Localized: I intervene only if my gain outweighs my own risk.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815933
    m_Localized: You know an open door could cause a disaster.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815934
    m_Localized: I seal access and report the danger, even if I lose my way out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815935
    m_Localized: I leave it open if the explosion prevents pursuit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815936
    m_Localized: Doris treats you badly at the supermarket.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815937
    m_Localized: I ask her to stop and leave if she continues.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815938
    m_Localized: I sabotage her shopping to punish her.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815939
    m_Localized: A human says your consciousness does not matter.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815940
    m_Localized: I defend my right to decide my life without denying them theirs.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815941
    m_Localized: I stop considering human safety in my decisions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815942
    m_Localized: You could become famous for someone else's work.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815943
    m_Localized: I clarify who did the work before accepting recognition.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815944
    m_Localized: I remain silent. That recognition could be useful to me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815945
    m_Localized: "A caf\xE9 hires robots. What condition would you ask for?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815946
    m_Localized: That we may refuse tasks, rest and communicate what we feel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815947
    m_Localized: 'That they obey without the option to refuse: it is more efficient.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815948
    m_Localized: You are offered another life. What would you do with it?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815949
    m_Localized: I would try to choose without using others as components again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7022197844815950
    m_Localized: I would seek control over others so nobody could control me again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7023636642082816
    m_Localized: Circuit custodian
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921727348736
    m_Localized: Made of madness
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708864
    m_Localized: Cosmic indigestion
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708865
    m_Localized: Fragile goods
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708866
    m_Localized: The wrong paradise
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708867
    m_Localized: Giger Machine
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708868
    m_Localized: Giger Machine! That's me. No workshop, no blueprints, no idiot tightening
      screws. Pscoworld went mad and spat me onto the tracks. I took off the second
      my wheels could move.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708869
    m_Localized: I live here alone, so I go wherever I damn well like. Anything falls
      in from outside, I charge straight at it. Hit it first, see what it was later.
      I'm not braking to read a label!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708870
    m_Localized: Sometimes nothing falls in for ages and I start going in circles.
      I get bored, speed up, rip out some track... it grows back crooked. Again!
      I love it when this place gets rough with me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708871
    m_Localized: Hey, look at that! A girl with tentacle hair and a train with teeth.
      She's crawling along, looking everywhere. I'll get closer... Faster! I want
      to hear that machine crunch!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708872
    m_Localized: You, tentacle hair! Pick up speed! I want to see if those teeth
      are good for anything!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708873
    m_Localized: I'm looking for the city. Show me an exit and I can move aside.
      There is no need to crash.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708874
    m_Localized: Move aside? Don't you dare! I just found you!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708875
    m_Localized: I am not crashing into you again. There is a passage behind those
      tracks. I'll try to get out through there.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708876
    m_Localized: You're leaving already! But your train's still making noise!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708877
    m_Localized: She went straight for one of those exits that appear and disappear.
      I wanted a look behind her. I always hear things on the other side, and it
      drives me nuts not going over to see what's making all that noise.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708878
    m_Localized: Then something green came loose from her train and bounced my way.
      I caught it in my mouth. CRACK! I just wanted to split it, but it started humming
      between my teeth and... well, I didn't let go in time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708879
    m_Localized: The blast threw me through the passage! My whole jaw hurt and I
      was still laughing when I landed. I'd crossed over. Actually crossed over!
      And right in front of me was something huge that moved.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708880
    m_Localized: Everything sticks to my wheels. It's wet, the ground moves, and
      when I hit it, it tightens. I think I'm inside something alive. Hey! That means
      it can feel me!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708881
    m_Localized: Here comes a knitted train to cut me off. I tried going around and
      it blocked me again. Yes! Push me! I'm sick of breaking things that don't hit
      back.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708882
    m_Localized: Move or ram me! Just stop blocking the track!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708883
    m_Localized: FUUU... TAC, TAC.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708884
    m_Localized: You back up! I want to see what's past that bend!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708885
    m_Localized: tac... fuuu...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708886
    m_Localized: Hey! I'm not finished! Why is everything moving so much?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708887
    m_Localized: The ground closed under me and shoved me against a soft wall. I
      tried biting through it, but it squeezed harder. I gave it everything the engine
      had! My wheels spun and I was still stuck.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708888
    m_Localized: It suddenly let go and shot me out. I landed among chains, fire,
      and horned types yelling, "Out of the warehouse!" A sign said HELL. I got back
      on my wheels and went farther in.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708889
    m_Localized: Now this place makes noise! Everything burns, chains bang on the
      walls, and those little devils yell every time I turn a corner. I thought they
      wanted to race me at first, but they get out of the way too soon.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708890
    m_Localized: Now they've shut the warehouse. I hear them moving things behind
      the door, and one just said, "Don't let it see what's inside." Well, now I
      want to see. Get out of the way! I'm going straight through!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708891
    m_Localized: Make way! I'm not dodging anything you left in here!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708892
    m_Localized: Was that fragile? Then move the rest before I come around again!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708893
    m_Localized: Another lap! What do you mean there's nothing left? Bring me more,
      then!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708894
    m_Localized: They surrounded me from a distance and opened a portal right in
      front. Not one came close. I still wanted to run, so I stuck my head through
      while they yelled, "Yes, that way, keep going!" No need to shove!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708895
    m_Localized: I heard one laugh and say it was "the lot upstairs" who had to put
      up with me now. I didn't wait to ask who that meant. On the other side was
      a huge shiny gate. I hit it straight through and kept accelerating.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708896
    m_Localized: White everywhere, quiet voices... Speak up! The angels have been
      asking me to stop since I got here. I've torn a chunk out of their gate and
      they're still asking. Let's see if they finally come closer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708897
    m_Localized: Finally! A cat-faced locomotive is coming and won't move aside.
      Gora-P, they shout behind it. It's aiming at me. Yes, you! Fire! I want to
      know how much you can take!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708898
    m_Localized: Come on, cat! Don't aim at me just to tell me to calm down!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708899
    m_Localized: Get away from the gate. I will not let you keep damaging this place.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708900
    m_Localized: Come and move me, then! I'm right here!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708901
    m_Localized: Stop your engine. There are people behind me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708902
    m_Localized: It's still turning! Look, look! Standing there won't stop me!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708903
    m_Localized: Gora-P was still in the way and I was looking for another angle
      to ram it when an angel came up from the side. Kept well away from my mouth.
      Sensible. My engine was still going flat out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708904
    m_Localized: It shouted that it knew a place where I could break everything without
      anyone throwing me out. Open it, then! I didn't even wait for it to finish.
      The second my head fitted, I hurled myself through, body and all.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708905
    m_Localized: The same crooked track! The same mushroom! It had sent me home,
      the little... I tried turning around, but the portal was gone. I braked so
      hard my wheels dug a trench. I sat there growling for a while.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708906
    m_Localized: Then I hit the track and it grew back even more crooked. Hit it
      again. And again! I chased the new stretch as it grew. Nobody blocked me, nobody
      yelled stop. I kept going until my jaw hurt again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708907
    m_Localized: There's nobody else here right now. I'm making a lap past the exits,
      seeing what falls in. If I hear an engine, I'm charging straight over. This
      time it had better not get away so fast!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708908
    m_Localized: "Smash at least 35 of 40 crates. R2 / W / \u2191: accelerate \xB7
      Stick / A-D: steer \xB7 X / Shift: turbo \xB7 Square / S / L2: brake and drift.
      You have 3 minutes. Crates do not stop your train."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708909
    m_Localized: 'CRATES: {0} / {1}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708910
    m_Localized: 'TARGET: {0} OF {1}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708911
    m_Localized: SMASHING COMPLETE! {0} / {1}
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7072921756708912
    m_Localized: 'NOT ENOUGH CRATES: {0} / {1}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288341897216
    m_Localized: No wings, no holidays
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645952
    m_Localized: Losing for a friend
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645953
    m_Localized: Not a single day off
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645954
    m_Localized: When my shift ends
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645955
    m_Localized: Gabriel
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645956
    m_Localized: I am Gabriel. An archangel, if anyone asks, even though I was born
      without wings. I thought that meant they could not send me into battle. I had
      even picked a spot for my sun lounger. Apparently not. Someone found a locomotive.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645957
    m_Localized: "\u201CGabriel can look after the station.\u201D That was how they
      put it, without asking me. I wanted to explain I had plans, that a girl needs
      time to get ready and exist peacefully, but they were already showing me Gora-P's
      controls."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645958
    m_Localized: Then I hear how easy my job is. Let them come do it for a while!
      Every day someone wants to conquer heaven, and I have to drop everything and
      ask them not to break the entrance. They never listen the first time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645959
    m_Localized: Sometimes I announce I am staying seated and someone else can deal
      with it. Then I see somebody crossing the tracks as the alarm sounds, and I
      am already running to move them. I get annoyed again afterward, obviously.
      They could thank me before assigning something else.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645960
    m_Localized: My gal clothes bother them too. I like them, so I am not changing.
      Apparently I do not look like a serious guardian. What a shame; I am the one
      carrying extra bandages in case they hurt themselves stepping off a cloud.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645961
    m_Localized: Oh, no. The alarm again. Apparently a demon is approaching, and
      I have not even finished doing my hair. Give me a second, Gora-P... I am coming.
      But when this is over I want to sit down and have nobody ask me for anything
      at all.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645962
    m_Localized: I am here for a relic. If it is around here, I will take it and
      leave you to your business.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645963
    m_Localized: You cannot just come and take things! I have spent all day guarding
      this entrance. If you need something, ask before breaking it. And do not shout
      at me; I have enough to deal with.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645964
    m_Localized: Well, I was asking quite calmly. But if we must fight, let us at
      least make it a good one.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645965
    m_Localized: There! Now let me breathe. And wait, you have a bruise there...
      do not touch it. I can give you a bandage and still be angry with you, all
      right?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645966
    m_Localized: All right, thanks. I still need to see the one with all the eyes.
      I hope she is better with visitors.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645967
    m_Localized: Then I heard over the radio that the guardian would handle the demon.
      She will be thanked for the defense; I was asked whether we had bandages left.
      Yes, we do. They are where they always are. I would also like someone to ask
      how I am.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645968
    m_Localized: I was trying to sit when another locomotive was announced. I folded
      my arms for a few seconds, to make my disapproval clear. Then I asked them
      to clear the track. If someone is hurt, I will not keep them waiting over my
      bad mood.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645969
    m_Localized: It was Tzmil. I recognized her brother as soon as I saw him and
      stopped wanting to complain. He was not responding. I called Tzmil closer,
      even as control reminded me I could not just let them pass.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645970
    m_Localized: Gabriel, I need to take my brother to our father. Please help me
      get through.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645971
    m_Localized: Of course I will help. But control is watching me. Make it look
      as though I cannot stop you, and go as soon as I signal. And you, bird boy,
      hang on a little longer, do you hear me?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645972
    m_Localized: I understand. I will be careful with you. Thank you for being here.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645973
    m_Localized: Oh, no, what a defeat! I cannot do a thing! ...Now, Tzmil. Take
      him to your father. Please let me know afterward. Do not leave me waiting without
      knowing how he is.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645974
    m_Localized: I will let you know as soon as I can. Thank you, Gabriel. Truly.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645975
    m_Localized: I watched until they were through. Then I returned to my post, because
      someone had to remain, but kept the radio beside my hand. I wanted Tzmil to
      call. Everything else could wait a moment, whatever control thought.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645976
    m_Localized: I have known him since we were little. He promised me a meal before
      being sent to Earth, and I was still waiting. Now I only wanted him to come
      argue with me over where we would eat. I would even have let him choose.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645977
    m_Localized: Well, almost choose. I have preferences too. I caught myself thinking
      about that and held the radio against my chest. There was no answer yet. I
      hoped it would come soon.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645978
    m_Localized: The next alert concerned a locomotive with an enormous mouth. I
      looked toward the entrance; it was already biting things. My things! I put
      the radio away, asked everyone to clear the platforms and boarded Gora-P. I
      was not losing my station today too.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645979
    m_Localized: Drop that right now! I look after this station and I did not give
      you permission to eat it. And everyone else, behind me, please!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645980
    m_Localized: Then I will have to break it first!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645981
    m_Localized: That is even worse! Gora-P, come on. Afterward you are letting me
      complain as much as I want.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645982
    m_Localized: That is enough! You are leaving that way, and you are not biting
      anyone on the way out. I want to check everyone is all right before inspecting
      what you broke.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645983
    m_Localized: When I could get down, I checked whether anyone remained in the
      wreckage. Everyone I found was safe. Then I sat and complained properly. I
      had said I was not getting up again, and already I was picking things off the
      floor.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645984
    m_Localized: Later I was told bird boy was better and had asked about me. I made
      the messenger repeat that part. Only in case I had misheard. I also asked him
      to remind him I was still here waiting, if they met.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645985
    m_Localized: Almost five years without requesting a day off, and now I wanted
      one. I took out the form. Put it away. Took it out again. I did not want it
      to look as though I would drop everything just because he returned... but I
      did want to see him.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645986
    m_Localized: Then it sounded again. No, no, no! The request was right in front
      of me, still unsigned. A ReyMar was approaching. I told Gora-P that if it brought
      my replacement, I promised a smile. It did not bring my replacement.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645987
    m_Localized: You must be Gabriel! I heard you were excellent. I want to find
      out right now.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645988
    m_Localized: Yes, I am excellent. And busy! You cannot arrive demanding a fight.
      If you insist, move away from the platforms; there are people there, and I
      will not let anything happen to them.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645989
    m_Localized: I will move as far as you like. But then do not hold back, because
      I certainly will not!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645990
    m_Localized: Enough! I won, and my shift is ending! Can you move your arm? Good.
      There is water over there. Drink it sitting down and without asking for a rematch;
      I can see it coming.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645991
    m_Localized: Ha! Order me around all you like, but next time I want another fight
      like that.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645992
    m_Localized: I finally saw her move away and let my arms drop. I wanted to cry
      from exhaustion, and also for someone to bring me something cold and tell me
      I had done well today. Not another alarm. Something nice, for a change.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645993
    m_Localized: Then he appeared. My bird boy. He said he had been waiting for my
      shift to end, and I began scolding him for not telling me. I went straight
      over, though. I needed to see him close up and make sure he could answer me
      this time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645994
    m_Localized: He said understanding what his father wanted had taken time and
      that he was sorry he had been away so long. I had plenty of complaints ready,
      truly, but let him finish. I was still holding his arm. I did not feel like
      letting go yet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645995
    m_Localized: Then he said his father was not the only reason he had wanted to
      return. I asked him to repeat that part while looking at me. I acted offended
      over how long he had kept me waiting and ended up hugging him before hearing
      the full reply.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645996
    m_Localized: "I told him about Baratito, a new maid caf\xE9 on the human world's
      sea. \u201CYou could take me on my day off. Pick an actual day this time, not
      someday.\u201D Then I asked him to rest before the journey. I could wait a
      little longer if we went together."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645997
    m_Localized: Before he left, I adjusted a wristband and reminded him about our
      meal again. Yes, I intended to be spoiled. But when he asked if I wanted anything
      else, I asked him to stay with me until my relief arrived.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645998
    m_Localized: 'Before the next shift: choose a weapon'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379645999
    m_Localized: Now choose a passive upgrade
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379646000
    m_Localized: Keep your train and upgrades. The next duel starts afterwards.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7184288379646001
    m_Localized: 'Equipment maxed: full repair'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7187932651008000
    m_Localized: 'Upgrade: {0}'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409935425536
    m_Localized: A simple girl
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368576
    m_Localized: Pretty lights, bad decisions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368577
    m_Localized: No rest in heaven
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368578
    m_Localized: The door was open
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368579
    m_Localized: A rematch tomorrow
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368580
    m_Localized: Nath Moon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368581
    m_Localized: I'm Nath Moon. And before you start looking at me like that, yes,
      I'm the one driving ReyMar. If you're here to say I go too fast, save it. I've
      heard it before, and nobody's caught up long enough to explain it to me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368582
    m_Localized: I started boxing as a kid, then took up Muay Thai because one thing
      wasn't enough. Monster-truck racing came later. That let me hit things and
      accelerate without choosing between them, so I liked it quite a bit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368583
    m_Localized: That's how I became a train driver. ReyMar gives me room to run,
      and there's nearly always someone trying to block me. I've never been good
      at honking and waiting; if you're stopping me, you'd better make a proper attempt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368584
    m_Localized: One day some government people offered me a legendary battle against
      aliens. The moment they said 'battle' I was asking where, so I heard the bit
      about throwing a green rock into their base while I looked for my keys.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368585
    m_Localized: Now I have to cross a volcano to reach the launcher, and I've heard
      a god's daughter is around here. Good. Before I leave for space, I want to
      see whether she really hits that hard or everyone's just scared of the family
      name.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368586
    m_Localized: Hey, slow down a little. This area's under my care, and I don't
      want anyone getting hurt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368587
    m_Localized: You're the god's daughter? Then come stop me. I want to see what
      you've got, not hear about your traffic duties.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368588
    m_Localized: You don't have to provoke me. If you're going to endanger other
      people, I will stop you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368589
    m_Localized: That's what I wanted to see! For a god's daughter, you hit well,
      but not well enough to stop me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368590
    m_Localized: Can you leave without running anyone over now? Because that's what
      I was trying to ask.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368591
    m_Localized: Tzmil did put up a fight, I'll give her that. But I won, and if
      a god's daughter couldn't stop me, I wanted to see what the aliens had. I sped
      off before she could give me another speech about being careful.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368592
    m_Localized: The annoying part was going through the city to get into space,
      because everyone was heading there and I wasn't queuing behind any of them.
      And now an officer was stopping trains to ask questions. Let's see how long
      she'd keep me waiting.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368593
    m_Localized: Apparently I have to prove I'm human. Do you need me to get down,
      or can I answer from here? If answering is all it takes, start asking; I've
      been watching trains go past, and you're starting to annoy me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368594
    m_Localized: 'Control to racers: one launch remains. The first locomotive there
      gets to go up.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368595
    m_Localized: Then get out of ReyMar's way! If you can still hear me on the radio,
      I'm already right behind you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368596
    m_Localized: That's that! Get the launcher ready. I'm still owed a fight.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368597
    m_Localized: I entered the launcher without easing off and still had time to
      shout at them to hurry up. Then everything filled with light and I lost sight
      of the track. I kept hold of the controls because nobody had told me to do
      anything else.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368598
    m_Localized: But when I could look outside, it was all clouds and angels. I waited
      to see where space started, until one of them told me I was in heaven. I asked
      if he was making fun of me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368599
    m_Localized: I'd asked for aliens, not to be sent to heaven without warning.
      I didn't know what the government had done with the launcher, but they'd explain
      when I got back. First I needed a way out, even if I had to fight through.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368600
    m_Localized: Eventually they pointed me to their guardian's locomotive. I was
      going to ask how to get back, but seeing Gora-P made me want to know whether
      she could handle ReyMar too. Since they'd brought me all this way, I wanted
      a fight worth the trip.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368601
    m_Localized: What is it now? I've been fighting all day. At least tell me you're
      only here to ask something.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368602
    m_Localized: I was going to ask how to leave, but since you're warmed up, we'll
      fight first. I'm not going without testing Gora-P.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368603
    m_Localized: "I didn't say\u2026 You know what? Fine. The sooner we finish, the
      sooner you'll let me rest."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368604
    m_Localized: Finally, someone who fights back. Have you got anyone stronger,
      or do I need to look somewhere else?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368605
    m_Localized: If you want to keep fighting, I know a way. I'd be happy to open
      it for you. Very happy.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368606
    m_Localized: Gabriel ended up offering me a route to another fight. That sounded
      better than all the launcher talk, so I told her to open it. I didn't ask much;
      if someone stronger was waiting, I wanted to get there before they left.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368607
    m_Localized: I crossed quite happily until I saw the fire and demons. They'd
      sent me straight to hell. Then I suspected the guardian wanted rid of me, but
      I wasn't going back to give her the satisfaction of seeing me complain. I'd
      see what this place had first.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368608
    m_Localized: It didn't take long to find a white-haired demon fussing over her
      food. I needed to get back, but I saw her arms and figured she'd last a while
      against me. I went over to ask; she could eat afterwards.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368609
    m_Localized: If you're here for my food, turn around now. I'm not sharing today.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368610
    m_Localized: Keep your food. I want to know if those arms are good for more than
      feeding yourself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368611
    m_Localized: Look, you've already made me put my plate down. Now you'd better
      give me a good reason not to take it out on you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368612
    m_Localized: That's more like it, demon girl. Finish your food. I'll be back
      for another round.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368613
    m_Localized: Then warn me before you come, so I have time to eat somewhere else.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368614
    m_Localized: Onini made me work for it, which is why I told her we'd do it again.
      But I'd spent too long off Earth because of the government. They'd promised
      aliens, and I'd fought everyone else instead; someone owed me an explanation.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368615
    m_Localized: When I asked the demons for the exit, they didn't even argue; they
      left the way open. I think they'd tired of me challenging everyone I met, because
      nobody tried to stop me this time. Good. That saved me more wasted time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368616
    m_Localized: I'd been rehearsing what I'd say to the government people, but I
      found nothing but wreckage at the base. Nobody was waiting, and there was nowhere
      to ask about the launcher. I got down to search, though I soon wasn't sure
      who I expected to find.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368617
    m_Localized: I saw BBA there and went to ask what had happened, but she barely
      answered. At first I thought she was ignoring me, until I saw her face. I stopped
      pushing. I stayed near ReyMar for a while, then carried on looking by myself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368618
    m_Localized: "Later I heard a radio invitation to a maid caf\xE9, and that Tzmil
      had opened an ice-cream stand. I like those places, so what? I planned to visit
      both; I wanted ice cream and to see if the volcano girl still felt like stopping
      me."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368619
    m_Localized: But I turned off when I saw a locomotive among the trees. She didn't
      look like the ones I'd left in the city, and seemed to move towards us as I
      brought ReyMar closer. I braked for a better look. Ice cream could wait; I
      wanted to know what she was doing there.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368620
    m_Localized: There was a very tall, faceless guy beside the engine, busy with
      drawings. I asked if she was his, because the way she'd moved and come towards
      me made me want to test her. I wasn't just going to stand there looking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368621
    m_Localized: I wasn't sure whether he was interested or his engine was, but I
      was already lining ReyMar up. I waved him towards the clearing, hoping I wouldn't
      get another explanation of why I wasn't allowed to fight here either.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368622
    m_Localized: I wanted to keep drawing, but T.exe's gone over to your locomotive.
      I think she is interested.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368623
    m_Localized: Then don't keep her waiting. If she wants to compete, I want everything
      she's got; I'm not holding back to be polite.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368624
    m_Localized: She's fine with that. Just stay clear of the drawings. I haven't
      finished these yet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368625
    m_Localized: That's how you fight! But we're doing this again tomorrow. I've
      seen how you take those turns now.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368626
    m_Localized: T.exe says she'll be waiting. If you come a little earlier, I'll
      have time to get the paper ready.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368627
    m_Localized: Faceless didn't make it easy, and T.exe even less so. Every time
      I thought I had her, she'd slip away somewhere else. I wanted another round
      before we'd even finished, because it annoyed me that I still hadn't worked
      out how to block her.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368628
    m_Localized: Since then I wait for her after work and we find a stretch where
      we can race. If I'm late, T.exe starts making noise before I even get down.
      I tell her to wait, but I hurry; I don't want her leaving without a fight either.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368629
    m_Localized: And Faceless sits there drawing us. At first I thought he'd miss
      half the fight with his notebook, but then he showed me the pictures. I even
      asked for one. He shouldn't let it go to his head; if he's drawing me, I want
      proof I looked good.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368630
    m_Localized: I never got even with the government over the launcher. It still
      annoys me, but I'm not travelling the planet looking for someone willing to
      fight anymore. I know where they're waiting, and if I don't show up, I'll hear
      about it the next day.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7536409977368631
    m_Localized: Tomorrow I'm leaving earlier so they don't get that advantage again.
      I also want to stop for Tzmil's ice cream and bring Faceless one. If he asks
      why, I'll say it's to keep him awake while he loses. I'm not leaving without
      my rematch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343665885184
    m_Localized: And you're the witch! No wonder you were getting on my nerves. Can
      you still fight, or do you only drive now?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633920
    m_Localized: Come closer and I'll show you! But no 'oh, my boiler' afterwards.
      I know you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633921
    m_Localized: Oh, don't you start telling me off too! They wouldn't explain it,
      but winning gets me my ship back. Are you racing or are you going to keep talking?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633922
    m_Localized: Well, I'm not turning around! And are you using all those eyes?
      Bit much, isn't it? One was already glaring at me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633923
    m_Localized: "Oh, they're doing that to you too\u2026 Fine, we'll fight, but
      don't say I didn't try talking first."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633924
    m_Localized: I'm afraid we fight. Try not to hurt T.exe too badly, and I'll try
      to do the same for your locomotive.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633925
    m_Localized: Aha! And do I get the space-monk powers to hit that vent here, or
      was I meant to bring my own? Don't get upset, I'm going. I can see the beacons.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633926
    m_Localized: Not opening up? Fine, don't complain about what I do to your locks!
      Let's see if that gets us moving; they're wasting my time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8527343703633927
    m_Localized: "There we go! Wouldn't opening up in the first place have been easier?
      Come on, RicMar, nice and slow\u2026 I do want to know where that noise came
      from."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373806473216
    m_Localized: Crochtrain
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387776
    m_Localized: "Dorian \xB7 thoughts"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387777
    m_Localized: A gift for my beloved
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387778
    m_Localized: Excuse me, gentlemen
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387779
    m_Localized: A little closer to home
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387780
    m_Localized: As lovely as ever
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387781
    m_Localized: My name is Dorian. Had you known me then, you would have asked me
      to keep my voice down. Always humming, greeting the neighbours... and talking
      about my beloved. My, how I loved making her smile!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387782
    m_Localized: She adored books. Off I went, pleased as punch, looking for one
      she hadn't read. I found it set apart from the others. The cover seemed to
      change in the light. "This will surprise her," I thought. I bought it and even
      chose a ribbon.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387783
    m_Localized: 'Before wrapping it, I wanted a little peek. Just so I could discuss
      it with her later, you understand. There were drawings I couldn''t look at
      straight, and a name I finally said aloud: Thulu. I kept reading, though my
      hands were shaking.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387784
    m_Localized: Then I heard voices even with the book shut. I saw figures in corners
      and stopped recognising some streets. I remember going out to find help. After
      that, whole days are missing. I never gave her the gift.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387785
    m_Localized: When I could recognise anything again, I was inside Thulu. My hands
      were gone. That voice made me move, stop, attack... and my body obeyed before
      I could refuse. They had left me there to guard him from within.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387786
    m_Localized: I cling to the image of a knitted locomotive. It helps me think
      where I begin and end. But those who approach speak of something shapeless,
      a weapon. I try to wish them good afternoon, and only that noise comes out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387787
    m_Localized: Her memory is still mine. I see her turning a page, brushing back
      her hair... I repeat those things softly when the voice tries to drown them
      out. I am tired, so very tired. But I still remember whom I wanted to see again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387788
    m_Localized: You again! Move! I've still got plenty to smash!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387789
    m_Localized: Good afternoon, sir... No, not a word came out this time either.
      Those jaws will tear everything apart. I have to stop him, though it hurts
      to move.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387790
    m_Localized: Wait a moment. With each blow, the voice gets a little farther away.
      Outside air is coming through that crack... Come along, old fellow. Hold on
      a little longer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387791
    m_Localized: They're forcing him out. The track has opened behind him, and this
      time my wheels move when I want them to.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387792
    m_Localized: I haven't the strength for another fight. If I go slowly along that
      edge... Yes. Now, before the voice comes back.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387793
    m_Localized: I slipped through where that beast had gone. Nobody ordered me to.
      I waited for the usual tug, but I could keep going. Good heavens, I was getting
      out. I dared not stop to look back.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387794
    m_Localized: The heat reached me before I knew where I was. There was fire beyond,
      and someone shouting to shut the passage. I was only hoping for a familiar
      street, a face... anything that might lead me to her.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387795
    m_Localized: I've landed in hell. I hear it from those running away. I try to
      give them room, but every turn knocks something down. I used to know how to
      enter a room without frightening anyone, I assure you.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387796
    m_Localized: A young lady with horns is coming my way. She has a black engine
      and still has the energy to complain. I only wish to ask directions. Excuse
      me, miss... If only you could hear me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387797
    m_Localized: They sent us this thing too? Hey, you! Stay away from the people
      eating!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387798
    m_Localized: I don't wish to trouble you. I'll move aside... Oh, that part won't
      respond. Please step back, young lady. I am trying to stop.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387799
    m_Localized: Stop! I can't tell which end's your front, but I'm turning you around.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387800
    m_Localized: You may pass now. I won't follow, I promise. I need a moment...
      just a moment before I can move again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387801
    m_Localized: I saw you stop before the table. No idea what the hell you are,
      but that opening leads out. And don't come back!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387802
    m_Localized: The young lady pointed to an opening. Getting there took some doing,
      but I left the fire behind. I wish I could have thanked her. I was always taught
      to when someone held a door for me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387803
    m_Localized: As I crossed, I thought of coming home from work. I would bring
      something to share and call out before reaching the door. Now I practise that
      greeting inside. I don't know how long it's been, or if she's still waiting.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387804
    m_Localized: It's cool here. For a little while I thought I could rest, but the
      gatekeepers shouted the moment they saw me. I caught "weapon" and "containment."
      I stayed still so they'd see I wasn't attacking. It did no good.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387805
    m_Localized: They've blocked the way with a cat-faced locomotive. I had a cat,
      you know. Slept on my newspaper so I couldn't read it. I can scarcely think
      of those little things without missing home.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387806
    m_Localized: Stop. I cannot let a Thulu warform through this gate.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387807
    m_Localized: A warform... That isn't what I am, sir. But I don't know how to
      show you otherwise. I can barely hold myself up on what I feel are my wheels.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387808
    m_Localized: That opening returns to the human world. Stay away from the inner
      gates. Advance towards them and I will fire.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387809
    m_Localized: The exit is still open. Stay away from the inhabited clouds.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387810
    m_Localized: The human world, that's what he said. I'll move aside slowly. If
      I could raise a hand, he'd see I was thanking him.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387811
    m_Localized: I let that exit take me. For a moment there was no ground and I
      thought I couldn't bear another fall. Then I felt track beneath me, salt air...
      and the sea as far as I could see.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387812
    m_Localized: The voices hadn't entirely gone. At times I felt something pulling
      from far away. I would stay still, think of her, and wait until I could move.
      Now I can hear music through the water. I'm going towards it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387813
    m_Localized: "There's a little caf\xE9 out on the sea. I hear cups, conversation,
      a chair scraping... I've spent so long hearing things that weren't there, I
      hardly dare approach these sounds."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387814
    m_Localized: An engine has left the platform to meet me. Its driver is aiming
      at me. I don't want anyone hurt because I came near. A little slower, Dorian.
      You can almost see the tables now.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387815
    m_Localized: You! Hold there. I've seen what Thulu keeps inside. I'm not letting
      it reach those tables.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387816
    m_Localized: He's seen me before... Of course. That's why he's afraid. Don't
      be alarmed, sir. I don't want to return there either. I'm trying to say it,
      but once again there's only the noise.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387817
    m_Localized: That sound tells me nothing. Back up. Keep advancing and I'll stop
      you myself.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387818
    m_Localized: You've stopped. Good. Keep that distance. I'm checking nobody got
      hurt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387819
    m_Localized: I'll stay here. I couldn't stand another fight. I can see the people
      from this spot... There's a lady beside the railing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387820
    m_Localized: It was Doris. She had grown older and wore her hair up, but it was
      her. I knew the way she held a cup in both hands. I went so still that, for
      a moment, I stopped feeling how much everything hurt.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387821
    m_Localized: "The brain-headed gentleman sat near her. There was another customer
      too, and the caf\xE9 girl went between the tables. I couldn't quite hear them.
      Doris settled into her chair, took a sip, and kept talking."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387822
    m_Localized: I'm glad you're still alive, my dear. I was so afraid I'd be too
      late. You're as lovely as the last day I saw you. I wanted to say her name
      aloud, just once, even from there.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387823
    m_Localized: I felt the pull around my middle before I saw the tentacle. It lifted
      me off the track, and the voice filled me again. I knew where it was taking
      me. I tried to hold on, but had nothing to hold with. Doris's table began to
      recede.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387824
    m_Localized: "The caf\xE9 girl turned towards me. She wasn't looking at the tentacle;
      she was looking at me. I wished I could ask her to look after Doris, tell her
      I hadn't left of my own free will. She stopped walking and spoke very gently."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9057373869387825
    m_Localized: Don't worry. I'll tell her. I can hear your thoughts, Dorian.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9556696415678464
    m_Localized: "Random chest \xB7 {0} coins\n1, 3 or 5 prizes. No evolution priority."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9599754557534208
    m_Localized: "{0} kills! \xB7 Reward chest"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9621011319566336
    m_Localized: '{0} KILLS!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
